<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1. </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The attention mechanism is a cornerstone of modern transformer architectures on which Large Language Models (LLMs) rely. Mathematically, an attention layer is a nonlinear operator <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}</annotation></semantics></math> that maps a collection of <em id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">tokens</em> <math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.338em;" width="0.338em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.338em;" width="0.338em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. This operator is parametrized by three (possibly sparse) <math id="S1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> matrices <math id="S1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K,Q," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K,Q,</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> and maps <math id="S1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,x^{\prime}_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,x^{\prime}_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> using the following formula. Define the normalization operator <math id="S1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(x)=x/\|x\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(x)=x/\|x\|</annotation></semantics></math> and for any <math id="S1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math> define <math id="S1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=QN(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=QN(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}=KN(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}=KN(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{\prime}=\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{\prime}=\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="S1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{\prime}=V\sum_{j=1}^{n}N(x_{j})A_{ij}\,,\qquad A_{ij}=\frac{e^{a_{ij}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{a_{ik}}}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{\prime}=V\sum_{j=1}^{n}N(x_{j})A_{ij}\,,\qquad A_{ij}=\frac{e^{a_{ij}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{a_{ik}}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the terms <math id="S1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}=q_{i}^{\top}k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}=q_{i}^{\top}k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are called <em id="S1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">attention scores</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A recent line of theoretical work has demonstrated that attention acts as a <em id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">contractive</em> operator that tends to cluster tokens together; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">DCL (21)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">GLPR (24)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">GLPR (25)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">KPR (24)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">GKPR (24)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">BPA25a ()</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">PRY (25)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">CLPR (25)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">CNQG (24)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">GG (25)</a></cite>. This clustering effect is also known as “rank-collapse” or “token uniformity” and arises because the distribution of attention scores tends to flatten as the sequence length <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> grows, causing each token to disperse its attention across too many other tokens rather than focusing selectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Various practical solutions have been proposed to curb this clustering behavior. In this work, we focus on simple context-length-aware modifications of the attention mechanism following ideas practically implemented as YaRN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">PQFS (23)</a></cite>, Qwen <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">BBC+ (23)</a></cite>, SSMax <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nak (25)</a></cite>, and SWAN-GPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">PLS+ (25)</a></cite>. These methods employ a straightforward strategy that rescales attention scores <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> by a single poly-logarithmic factor <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>; see Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Our goal in this paper is to answer the following fundamental question:</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">What is the optimal order of magnitude of the <math id="S1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> scaling?</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.T1" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:39%;">
<table id="S1.T1.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S1.T1.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T1.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Method</th>
<th id="S1.T1.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="S1.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> scaling</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S1.T1.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T1.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">YaRN</th>
<td id="S1.T1.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S1.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\log n)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\log n)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T1.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T1.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Qwen</th>
<td id="S1.T1.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log n</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T1.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T1.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">SSMax</th>
<td id="S1.T1.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log n</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T1.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T1.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">SWAN-GPT</th>
<td id="S1.T1.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S1.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log n</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S1.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>. </span><span id="S1.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Attention scaling factors for various methods. The standard attention score <math id="S1.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(k_{i}^{\top}q_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(k_{i}^{\top}q_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced with <math id="S1.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(C\beta_{n}k_{i}^{\top}q_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(C\beta_{n}k_{i}^{\top}q_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To address this question, we propose a highly simplified yet completely tractable model for attention. This model exhibits a phase transition governed by the parameter <math id="S1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>: when <math id="S1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is below a critical threshold, attention becomes overly contractive and collapses all tokens to a single direction, while when <math id="S1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is too large, attention acts as an identity operator and fails to process information effectively. More precisely, we establish that the critical parameter <math id="S1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> scales as <math id="S1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log n</annotation></semantics></math>, which corroborates the empirical guidelines underlying YaRN, Qwen, SSMax, and SWAN-GPT.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Our work is intimately connected to the recent contributions of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">CNQG (24)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">GG (25)</a></cite>, who investigate the contractive effects of attention mechanisms with random key and query matrices <math id="S1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> to establish proper initialization schemes for these parameters. A crucial insight from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">CNQG (24)</a></cite> is that analyzing the evolution of symmetric token configurations provides a more mathematically tractable framework compared to the generic input distributions considered in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">GLPR (25)</a></cite>. This symmetric setting, while simplified, captures essential dynamics of the attention mechanism and enables rigorous theoretical analysis; see also <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">KGPR (25)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The choice <math id="S1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> appears natural in retrospect. As noted in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nak (25)</a></cite>, with such a scaling the attention weights <math id="S1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) become</p>
<table id="S1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}=\frac{n^{\gamma a_{ij}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}n^{\gamma a_{ik}}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}=\frac{n^{\gamma a_{ij}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}n^{\gamma a_{ik}}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">To illustrate the resulting dynamics, consider a simplified regime where all attention scores <math id="S1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> are of order one: specifically, let <math id="S1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ii}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ii}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}=\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}=\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>. In this setting, the off-diagonal weights satisfy</p>
<table id="S1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}=\frac{n^{\gamma\rho}}{n^{\gamma}+(n-1)n^{\gamma\rho}}\sim\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\nicefrac{{1}}{{n}}&amp;\text{if }\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}\\
\nicefrac{{1}}{{n^{\gamma(1-\rho)}}}&amp;\text{if }\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}\\
\end{array}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mi mathsize="0.700em">n</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">n</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.710em" minsize="0.710em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">ρ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.710em" minsize="0.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}=\frac{n^{\gamma\rho}}{n^{\gamma}+(n-1)n^{\gamma\rho}}\sim\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}\nicefrac{{1}}{{n}}&amp;\text{if }\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}\\
\nicefrac{{1}}{{n^{\gamma(1-\rho)}}}&amp;\text{if }\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}\\
\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">This analysis reveals two distinct regimes. When <math id="S1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is small (subcritical regime), attention weights are asymptotically uniform, resulting in diffuse attention that, as we demonstrate below, leads to severe token contraction. Conversely, when <math id="S1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is large (supercritical regime), off-diagonal weights become negligible with respect to the diagonal ones so that the attention mechanism is effectively suppressed.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The critical regime emerges at the phase boundary <math id="S1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> where attention can concentrate on a sublinear yet nontrivial number of tokens so as to maintain sufficient connections to facilitate information flow from a small set of important tokens. This sparse attention is related to structured attention mechanisms employed in long-context architectures such as Longformer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">BPC (20)</a></cite> and SWIN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">LLC+ (21)</a></cite> which implement a sliding window over <math id="S1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\ll n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\ll n</annotation></semantics></math>-nearest neighbors but where proximity is measured in terms of token position rather than embedding. Unlike these structurally constrained approaches that rely on fixed positional neighborhoods, the logarithmic scaling enables the attention pattern to be entirely <em id="S1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">content-adaptive</em>, allowing each token to dynamically select its most relevant context based on semantic similarity rather than positional proximity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Following similar motivations, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">GG (25)</a></cite>
establish a compelling analogy between attention dynamics and the random energy model from
statistical physics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Der (81)</a></cite>. Using the replica method—an analytical heuristic
from statistical physics—they identify a phase transition occurring at <math id="S1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}\sim\sqrt{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}\sim\sqrt{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which differs from the scalings presented in Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. This result represents
a significant discrepancy from our findings and highlights fundamental differences in modeling assumptions.
More specifically, their approach assumes that the attention scores <math id="S1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> are correlated
Gaussian random variables. This assumption effectively induces a random geometry on the token
space, where similarity between tokens is treated as fundamentally random. In this sense,
their model bears closer resemblance to recent Kuramoto models on random graphs studied
in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">ABK+ (22)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">JMS (25)</a></cite>, where the authors investigate the synchronization
of oscillators interacting across the edges of a (sparse) Erdős–Rényi random graph
with unit edge weights.
However, in the case of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">GG (25)</a></cite>, the random graph
is both directed and dense, with the edge pointing from token <math id="S1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> to token <math id="S1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> having weight
given by</p>
<table id="S1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}=\frac{e^{\beta_{n}a_{ij}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{\beta_{n}a_{ik}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}=\frac{e^{\beta_{n}a_{ij}}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{\beta_{n}a_{ik}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> are Gaussian random variables. While <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">GG (25)</a></cite> assumes a specific correlation structure between the Gaussian random variables, the phase transition they uncover is expected to be universal within a large class of random matrices including Wigner ones.
Crucially though, in such models, the interaction strength <math id="S1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>
is independent of the positional relationship between tokens <math id="S1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, making this model
qualitatively different from standard attention mechanisms where attention is focused on few (or all) of the preceding tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">BPA25b ()</a></cite> adopt a different approach to studying the regime where <math id="S1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, in a more general setting than ours. By considering various levels of generality for the matrices <math id="S1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K,Q,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K,Q,V</annotation></semantics></math>, this work identifies distinct regimes of token dynamics and relates them to the hardmax (<math id="S1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>) limit. Importantly, the analysis is conducted in the subcritical regime and differs from the present work in focusing on a broader class of models, for which the critical regime has yet to be precisely characterized. We believe that combining the analytical tools developed in both papers could yield a deeper understanding of this critical regime and represents a promising direction for future research.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The remainder of the paper is organized as follows.
Section <a href="#S2" title="2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> provides a precise mathematical formulation of the phase transition phenomena for the rescaled attention layer. We begin by analyzing token angles and the contractive behavior of tokens under two settings: an idealized but intuitive simplex model (Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>) and a more realistic model with the simplex constraint relaxed (Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>). In both cases, we identify three distinct regimes of the scaling parameter, each leading to qualitatively different contrastive behaviors of the self-attention layer.
Section <a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> turns to the gradient norm of the rescaled attention operator. Because rank collapse is often accompanied by vanishing gradients, we characterize the gradient dynamics across scaling regimes and show when gradients vanish, or stabilize to non-trivial limits.
Section <a href="#S3" title="3. Numerical Experiments ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents our numerical experiments, which validate these theoretical predictions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this paper, when we denote a quantity as <math id="S1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of tokens, we mean there are positive constants <math id="S1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> independent of the dimension <math id="S1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="S1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|o_{n}(1)|\leq C_{1}n^{-C_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|o_{n}(1)|\leq C_{1}n^{-C_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The constants <math id="S1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> depend on the assumptions in theorems.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2. </span>A phase transition for attention</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we establish the main theorem of this paper, namely a phase transition for the contractive properties of the attention layer when <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">GLPR (25)</a></cite>, we study a simplified version of the attention layer with pre-layer norm that is described in the introduction by assuming that <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=Q=V=I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=Q=V=I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. More specifically, the model we study is given as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For any two points <math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.338em;" width="0.338em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x,y\rangle=x^{\top}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x,y\rangle=x^{\top}y</annotation></semantics></math> denote the standard Euclidean inner product in <math id="S2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.338em;" width="0.338em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|=\sqrt{\langle x,x\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|=\sqrt{\langle x,x\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, recall that <math id="S2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(x)\coloneqq x/\|x\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(x)\coloneqq x/\|x\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For any collection of tokens <math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.338em;" width="0.338em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="S2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}=N(x_{i})\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}=N(x_{i})\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{i}\coloneqq\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{a_{ik}}\,,\qquad A_{ij}\coloneqq\frac{e^{a_{ij}}}{Z_{i}}\,,\qquad a_{ij}\coloneqq\beta\left\langle y_{i},y_{j}\right\rangle\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{i}\coloneqq\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{a_{ik}}\,,\qquad A_{ij}\coloneqq\frac{e^{a_{ij}}}{Z_{i}}\,,\qquad a_{ij}\coloneqq\beta\left\langle y_{i},y_{j}\right\rangle\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">for <math id="S2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then define</p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})\coloneqq\sum_{j=1}^{n}A_{ij}y_{j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})\coloneqq\sum_{j=1}^{n}A_{ij}y_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Since the seminal work of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">HZRS (16)</a></cite>, residual connections are added to modern architectures and naturally act as a regularization scheme of the attention map towards the identity; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">CLC+ (25)</a></cite>. With said residual connections, each token <math id="S2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is mapped to <math id="S2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> using the following update rule</p>
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}^{\prime}\coloneqq\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})+\alpha x_{i}\,,\qquad\alpha\geq 0\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}^{\prime}\coloneqq\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})+\alpha x_{i}\,,\qquad\alpha\geq 0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Our first goal is to understand where the angle <math id="S2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\measuredangle(x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\measuredangle(x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> compares to <math id="S2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\measuredangle(x_{i},x_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\measuredangle(x_{i},x_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\measuredangle(x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime})&lt;\measuredangle(x_{i},x_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∡</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\measuredangle(x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime})&lt;\measuredangle(x_{i},x_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>—or equivalently <math id="S2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle&gt;\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle&gt;\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}^{\prime}=N(x_{i}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}^{\prime}=N(x_{i}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>—we say that attention is <em id="S2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">contractive</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The nonlinear update rule (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>) can produce complex dynamics, in which some pairs of tokens move closer together while others drift apart. This diversity of motion is in fact the most desirable outcome in practice, and it emerges precisely at the phase transition identified in this study. Beyond this critical regime, the tokens exhibit an unexpectedly cohesive behavior. To delineate the boundaries of the critical regime, we assume that the size and relative positions of the initial tokens are governed by constants independent of the number <math id="S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> of tokens. As an analytically tractable extreme of this assumption, we first consider the case in which the tokens form a regular simplex in <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">CNQG (24)</a></cite>. Despite its symmetry, this configuration is sufficient to capture and predict the onset of the phase transition. We subsequently relax this constraint in Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> to show that the same phase transition occurs in more realistic configurations.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1. </span>The simplex case</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following assumption was made in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">CNQG (24)</a></cite> and subsequently in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">GG (25)</a></cite>. While rather stringent—in particular, it requires <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq n</annotation></semantics></math>—it turns out to provide a tractable yet predictive setup to study the contractive properties of attention.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists nonnegative constants <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}\|^{2}=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}\|^{2}=q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle=\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, it is easy to see that there are positive constants <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\rho^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\rho^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}^{\prime}\|^{2}=q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}^{\prime}\|^{2}=q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. This simplification gives rise to a tractable phase transition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, there is a <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{\prime}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{\prime}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\rho^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\rho^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, if <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant, then for any <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\begin{cases}\frac{\rho(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}}{\alpha^{2}q+2\alpha\sqrt{q}\rho+\rho}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{\rho(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}}{\alpha^{2}q+\alpha\sqrt{q}(1+\rho)+\frac{1+3\rho}{4}}&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\rho&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>ρ</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\begin{cases}\frac{\rho(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}}{\alpha^{2}q+2\alpha\sqrt{q}\rho+\rho}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{\rho(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}}{\alpha^{2}q+\alpha\sqrt{q}(1+\rho)+\frac{1+3\rho}{4}}&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\rho&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note that when <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\leq\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\leq\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, the right hand sides of (<a href="#S2.E4" title="Equation 2.4 ‣ Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>) are strictly larger than <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, in the critical and subcritical regimes attention is contractive even in the presence of a residual connection. Of course, when <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the effects of attention dissipates and the limit tends to <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> for all phases. This is expected as the update from <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> tends to the identity map, an effect known to “mitigate oversmoothing” in residual neural networks; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">CLC+ (25)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Note also that for <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>, that is in absence of residual connections, the limit in (<a href="#S2.E4" title="Equation 2.4 ‣ Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>) reduces to</p>
<table id="S2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{4\rho}{1+3\rho}&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\rho&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>ρ</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{4\rho}{1+3\rho}&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\rho&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In the subcritical case, the tokens contract in one step towards a single cluster when <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> while in the supercritical case, their inner product does not change. In fact, a careful inspection of the proof reveals that in this supercritical regime the attention operator converges to the identity as <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the subcritical case is mitigated by the residual connection which prevents token to collapse to a single point in one step. Nevertheless, this singular behavior reveals a major limitation in the simplex case: since the tokens are equidistant the phase transition reveals an all-or-nothing phenomenon where attention transitions from <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}\sim 1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}\sim 1/n</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=\bar{y}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}y_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=\bar{y}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}y_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}=\delta_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}=\delta_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. In the next section, we present a similar result Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, where the simplex assumption is relaxed.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Before we end this section, we present the proof for (<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 2.5 ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>) as a special case of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>. The detailed proof for Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and the later Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> in Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> is included in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of (<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 2.5 ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>).</h6>
<div id="S2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">In (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>), when <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{\prime}=\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{\prime}=\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. In (<a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 2.1 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>), under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we notice that the quantity <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{a_{ik}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{a_{ik}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the denominator of <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of the choice of <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and equals to <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta}+(n-1)e^{\rho\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta}+(n-1)e^{\rho\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote this as <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\coloneqq e^{\beta}+(n-1)e^{\rho\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\coloneqq e^{\beta}+(n-1)e^{\rho\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then (<a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2.2 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>) become</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}^{\prime}=\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=\frac{1}{Z}\left(e^{\beta}y_{i}+\sum_{m\neq i}e^{\rho\beta}y_{m}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}^{\prime}=\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=\frac{1}{Z}\left(e^{\beta}y_{i}+\sum_{m\neq i}e^{\rho\beta}y_{m}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, a direct computation shows that for any <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=\frac{1}{Z^{2}}\left(e^{2\beta}+2(n-1)\rho e^{(1+\rho)\beta}+(n-1)(1+(n-2)\rho)e^{2\rho\beta}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=\frac{1}{Z^{2}}\left(e^{2\beta}+2(n-1)\rho e^{(1+\rho)\beta}+(n-1)(1+(n-2)\rho)e^{2\rho\beta}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">and for any two different <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j=1,2,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j=1,2,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\frac{1}{Z^{2}}\left(\rho e^{2\beta}+2(1+(n-2)\rho)e^{\beta(1+\rho)}+\left((n-2)+(n^{2}-3n+3)\rho\right)e^{2\beta\rho}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\frac{1}{Z^{2}}\left(\rho e^{2\beta}+2(1+(n-2)\rho)e^{\beta(1+\rho)}+\left((n-2)+(n^{2}-3n+3)\rho\right)e^{2\beta\rho}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">See also Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> for more detailed computations for <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=e^{\beta}+(n-1)e^{\rho\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=e^{\beta}+(n-1)e^{\rho\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, when we let <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta}=n^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta}=n^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ne^{\rho\beta}=n^{1+\rho\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ne^{\rho\beta}=n^{1+\rho\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>. The largest term in <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> then depends on the relation between <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\rho\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\rho\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>: when <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{1+\rho\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{1+\rho\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> is the largest term; when <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> is the largest term. We then directly get the following three phases for <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> from the above arguments:</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z=\begin{cases}(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot ne^{\rho\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
(2+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z=\begin{cases}(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot ne^{\rho\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
(2+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the terms <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> go to <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, we can get the the following three phases for <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=\begin{cases}\rho&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{1+3\rho}{4}&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
1&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>ρ</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=\begin{cases}\rho&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{1+3\rho}{4}&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
1&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, we always have that <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\rho</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> in these three different regimes. Then (<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 2.5 ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>) follows from these two limits since <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\langle x_{i}^{\prime}/\|x_{i}^{\prime}\|,x_{j}^{\prime}/\|x_{j}^{\prime}\|\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\langle x_{i}^{\prime}/\|x_{i}^{\prime}\|,x_{j}^{\prime}/\|x_{j}^{\prime}\|\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2. </span>The almost-simplex case</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we relax Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to allow pairwise angles and lengths to vary slightly. This relaxation makes it possible for tokens to lie in a dimension <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\ll n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\ll n</annotation></semantics></math>. Although the resulting bounds are not as sharp as those obtained under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, they demonstrate that the critical scaling <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}=\Theta(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}=\Theta(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> is intrinsic and not merely an artifact of a particular geometric construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist constants <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1},q_{2}\in(0,\infty),\rho_{1},\rho_{2}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1},q_{2}\in(0,\infty),\rho_{1},\rho_{2}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}\leq\|x_{i}\|^{2}\leq q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}\leq\|x_{i}\|^{2}\leq q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{1}\leq\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle\leq\rho_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{1}\leq\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle\leq\rho_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{1}=\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{1}=\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is easy to see using standard probabilistic tools that Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> holds with high probability when the <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are independent random vectors uniformly distributed on a half-sphere for example.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2.2</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we have the following phase transition when <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> for some fixed <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then there is a constant <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> depending on <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\rho_{2},q_{1},q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\rho_{2},q_{1},q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varliminf_{n\to+\infty}\min_{i\neq j}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle\geq\rho_{1}+\varepsilon&gt;\rho_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>lim</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varliminf_{n\to+\infty}\min_{i\neq j}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle\geq\rho_{1}+\varepsilon&gt;\rho_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which implies that the angle between tokens becomes strictly smaller after an attention layer (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=y_{i}+o_{n}(1),\text{ and hence }x_{i}^{\prime}=y_{i}+\alpha x_{i}+o_{n}(1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and hence </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=y_{i}+o_{n}(1),\text{ and hence }x_{i}^{\prime}=y_{i}+\alpha x_{i}+o_{n}(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the term <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> goes to <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> with a speed uniform in <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, when <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any two different <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which implies that the angle between tokens does not change after an attention layer (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The proof for Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> is included in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, but the general intuition is similar to the proof for (<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 2.5 ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>) in Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>. As we have seen in that proof, the first step to build up phase transition regimes for <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is to study the phase transition regimes for <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 2.1 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>). Adjusting the logarithmic scaling factor <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> causes different phase transition regimes for <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> first. When <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is small enough, the weights <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{a_{ik}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{a_{ik}}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are asymptotically uniform, and each token almost equally interacts with the other tokens. When <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough, each token mostly focuses on itself.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Building on this observation, Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> together demonstrate that <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> controls the effective interaction range of each token. In particular, we have seen in Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> the existence of the critical regime when <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, although the tokens continue to contract, their rate of shrinkage is evidently slower than in the subcritical regime, as shown in (<a href="#S2.E4" title="Equation 2.4 ‣ Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 2.5 ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">It is hence natural to ask whether further regimes emerge when <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is varied between the supercritical and subcritical threshold. Indeed, in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Modified Assumptions with More Median Phases ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>, we prove the existence of a nontrivial middle phase when <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is between the two extrema <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, under a refined assumption on the distribution of tokens, which allows for a sharper characterization of the transition. Under this refined assumption, Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem C.2. ‣ Appendix C Modified Assumptions with More Median Phases ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> show the existence of <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>) presents three different phases: <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}&lt;\gamma&lt;\gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}&lt;\gamma&lt;\gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the extreme regimes, when <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, each token interacts with almost all the remaining tokens, while when <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, each token only focuses on itself, consistent with Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>. In the intermediate regime <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}&lt;\gamma&lt;\gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}&lt;\gamma&lt;\gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, however, the weights <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{a_{ik}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{a_{ik}}</annotation></semantics></math> concentrate on only a small subset of tokens, so that each <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence the update in (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>) is dominated by a few highly relevant interactions. This shows that the logarithmic scaling enables each token to dynamically select its most relevant context.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We conclude by noting that those <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> terms in our theorems satisfy the bound <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|o_{n}(1)|\leq C_{1}n^{-C_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|o_{n}(1)|\leq C_{1}n^{-C_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some positive constants <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> that are independent of <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> (though varying across theorems). As a result, the simplex configuration (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and the almost simplex configuration (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) remains valid under repeated application of the <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}</annotation></semantics></math> operator up to <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{poly}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{poly}(n)</annotation></semantics></math> iterations. In particular, the accumulated error remains negligible at this scale, so our theorems and arguments extend to transformers with many layers.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3. </span>Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the previous section, we established how attention scaling influences the propagation of token representations, corresponding to running the Transformer in the forward (inference) direction. During training, however, the Transformer is also executed in the <em id="S2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">backward</em> direction to compute gradients via backpropagation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">RHW (86)</a></cite>. In this section, we show that a similar phase transition arises in the backward pass: in the subcritical regime—where token representations rapidly collapse in the forward pass—the gradients also collapse, whereas in the supercritical regime they retain their scale. The stability of gradients is a crucial computational consideration that strongly affects a model’s ability to be trained effectively. For this reason, several theoretical analyses of gradient dynamics in Transformers have been conducted, albeit without attention scaling; see, for example, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">CNQG (24)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">DCL (21)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">NAB+ (22)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let the input token configuration be denoted by <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(0)</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(t)</annotation></semantics></math> represent the positions of all tokens at the output of Transformer layer <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. To compute gradients, one needs to evaluate the end-to-end input–output Jacobian across <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers of the Transformer. By the chain rule, this Jacobian can be expressed as</p>
<table id="S2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial X(L)}{\partial X(0)}=\frac{\partial X(L)}{\partial X(L-1)}\frac{\partial X(L-1)}{\partial X(L-2)}\cdots\frac{\partial X(1)}{\partial X(0)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial X(L)}{\partial X(0)}=\frac{\partial X(L)}{\partial X(L-1)}\frac{\partial X(L-1)}{\partial X(L-2)}\cdots\frac{\partial X(1)}{\partial X(0)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the end-to-end Jacobian can be obtained by recursively computing and multiplying the layer-wise Jacobians. This procedure is known as the <em id="S2.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adjoint method</em> in dynamical systems theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lio (71)</a></cite>, and as <em id="S2.SS3.p2.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">backpropagation</em> in the machine learning community.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our main result shows that when <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> with subcritical <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the typical singular values of <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial X(t+1)}{\partial X(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial X(t+1)}{\partial X(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> are close to zero (apart from the contribution of the residual connection). In contrast, for supercritical values of <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the contribution of the attention component to the Jacobian is non-trivial and behaves as a normalization map.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We now proceed with formal definitions. For <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.338em;" width="0.338em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x)_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x)_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> denote its <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>-th coordinate for <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=1,2,\dots,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=1,2,\dots,d</annotation></semantics></math>. The concatenation <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(x_{1},x_{2},\dots,x_{n})\in{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{nd}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.338em;" width="0.338em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(x_{1},x_{2},\dots,x_{n})\in{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{nd}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the configuration of all tokens. The normalization map is defined by</p>
<table id="S2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(X)=\mathcal{N}(x_{1},x_{2},\dots,x_{n})\coloneqq\big(N(x_{1}),N(x_{2}),\dots,N(x_{n})\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(X)=\mathcal{N}(x_{1},x_{2},\dots,x_{n})\coloneqq\big(N(x_{1}),N(x_{2}),\dots,N(x_{n})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">and the attention map by</p>
<table id="S2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{ATT}(Y)=\mathcal{ATT}(y_{1},y_{2},\dots,y_{n})\coloneqq\big(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{1}),\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{2}),\dots,\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{n})\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{ATT}(Y)=\mathcal{ATT}(y_{1},y_{2},\dots,y_{n})\coloneqq\big(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{1}),\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{2}),\dots,\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{n})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in (<a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2.2 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>) and <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under these definitions, the update (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>) can be written compactly as</p>
<table id="S2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X^{\prime}=\mathcal{ATT}(\mathcal{N}(X))+\alpha X," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X^{\prime}=\mathcal{ATT}(\mathcal{N}(X))+\alpha X,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}=(x_{1}^{\prime},x_{2}^{\prime},\dots,x_{n}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}=(x_{1}^{\prime},x_{2}^{\prime},\dots,x_{n}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We define the <math id="S2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nd\times nd" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nd\times nd</annotation></semantics></math> Jacobian matrix as</p>
<table id="S2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\coloneqq\left(\frac{\partial(x_{j}^{\prime})_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{(j,v),(i,u)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\coloneqq\left(\frac{\partial(x_{j}^{\prime})_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{(j,v),(i,u)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">for <math id="S2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v=1,\ldots,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v=1,\ldots,d</annotation></semantics></math>.
The matrix norm of <math id="S2.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}\coloneqq\mathrm{tr}\!\left[(\nabla_{X}X^{\prime})^{\top}\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\right]=\sum_{i,j=1}^{n}\sum_{u,v=1}^{d}\left(\frac{\partial(x_{j}^{\prime})_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.670em;" width="0.670em"><mi>tr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}\coloneqq\mathrm{tr}\!\left[(\nabla_{X}X^{\prime})^{\top}\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\right]=\sum_{i,j=1}^{n}\sum_{u,v=1}^{d}\left(\frac{\partial(x_{j}^{\prime})_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2},\dots,\sigma_{nd}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2},\dots,\sigma_{nd}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the singular values of <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the normalized Jacobian norm satisfies</p>
<table id="S2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{nd}\sum_{i=1}^{nd}\sigma_{i}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{nd}\sum_{i=1}^{nd}\sigma_{i}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">which represents the mean squared singular value of the Jacobian.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Before stating our results on <math id="S2.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we note that the Jacobian <math id="S2.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> can be decomposed into the residual part <math id="S2.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha I_{nd}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha I_{nd}</annotation></semantics></math> and the attention part <math id="S2.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{X}\!\big(\mathcal{ATT}(\mathcal{N}(X))\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{X}\!\big(\mathcal{ATT}(\mathcal{N}(X))\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.
As shown in Theorems <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, the residual component <math id="S2.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha I_{nd}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha I_{nd}</annotation></semantics></math> does not affect the phase transition behavior.
Therefore, to streamline the analysis, we focus exclusively on the attention term <math id="S2.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{X}\!\big(\mathcal{ATT}(\mathcal{N}(X))\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{X}\!\big(\mathcal{ATT}(\mathcal{N}(X))\big)</annotation></semantics></math> by setting <math id="S2.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E13" title="Equation 2.13 ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>).
The following theorems characterize <math id="S2.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> under this setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2.3</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Adopt Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E13" title="Equation 2.13 ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>) with <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have the following phase transition phenomenon: let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=0+o_{n}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=0+o_{n}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{4q}\left(1-\frac{1}{d}\right)+o_{n}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{4q}\left(1-\frac{1}{d}\right)+o_{n}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{q}\left(1-\frac{1}{d}\right)+o_{n}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{q}\left(1-\frac{1}{d}\right)+o_{n}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In both cases, the terms <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> go to <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, with speeds depending on <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho,q</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The results of the previous theorem show that under the simplex assumption, the phase transition in the backward dynamics (for gradients) is as sharp as for the forward pass: for small <math id="S2.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, gradients do not flow through the attention block.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We can also extend the analysis for Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> to the relaxed Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2.4</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Adopt Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E13" title="Equation 2.13 ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>) with <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have the following phase transition phenomenon: let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}\leq 4\frac{\gamma^{2}(\log(n))^{2}}{q_{1}d}+o_{n}(1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}\leq 4\frac{\gamma^{2}(\log(n))^{2}}{q_{1}d}+o_{n}(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}\geq\frac{1}{q_{2}}\left(1-\frac{1}{d}\right)+o_{n}(1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}\geq\frac{1}{q_{2}}\left(1-\frac{1}{d}\right)+o_{n}(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which is away from <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> even when <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,n</annotation></semantics></math> is very large. Indeed, when <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any fixed <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{d\times d}=\frac{\delta_{ij}}{\|x_{i}\|}\left(I_{d}-y_{i}y_{i}^{T}\right)+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)+o_{n}(1)\cdot I_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{d\times d}=\frac{\delta_{ij}}{\|x_{i}\|}\left(I_{d}-y_{i}y_{i}^{T}\right)+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)+o_{n}(1)\cdot I_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the leading order term is exactly <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial(N(x_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial(N(x_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> as shown in Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>. Here, <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> identity matrix, the term <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively) is a <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> matrix (constant, respectively) with matrix norm as defined in (<a href="#S2.E15" title="Equation 2.15 ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.15</span></a>) (value, respectively) going to <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, with a speed independent of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math> but only depending on <math id="S2.Thmtheorem4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho_{2},q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho_{2},q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We present the proofs for Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>. Note that the <math id="S2.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log^{2}n\over d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log^{2}n\over d</annotation></semantics></math> term in (<a href="#S2.E20" title="Equation 2.20 ‣ Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.20</span></a>) is small for typical values of <math id="S2.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> used in Transformers. Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a> also corroborate the fact that tokens collapse fast when <math id="S2.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is in the subcritical regime, while each token only focuses on itself when <math id="S2.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is in the supercritical regime.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3. </span>Numerical Experiments</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section reports numerical experiments designed to corroborate our theoretical predictions. In the following numerical experiments, we test the phase transition in the almost-simplex case as Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>. We generate samples <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the expectations <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|x_{i}\|^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|x_{i}\|^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\langle x_{i},x_{j}\rangle=\rho\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\langle x_{i},x_{j}\rangle=\rho\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>. More precisely, we generate <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> according to</p>
<table id="S3.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}=\sqrt{\rho}\,z_{0}+\sqrt{1-\rho}\,z_{i}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}=\sqrt{\rho}\,z_{0}+\sqrt{1-\rho}\,z_{i}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0},z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0},z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. standard Gaussian vectors in <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. The generated samples satisfy the Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with high probability.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 3. Numerical Experiments ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we plot the input-to-output angle ratio <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as</p>
<table id="S3.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda=\frac{2}{n(n-1)}\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq n}\frac{1-\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle}{1-\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda=\frac{2}{n(n-1)}\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq n}\frac{1-\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle}{1-\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">for samples processed through a single self-attention layer with different <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and of different dimensions <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. Consistent with our theoretical predictions, the layer acts as a contraction mapping when <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is small, reducing pairwise output angles, whereas for large <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> the output angles remain nearly unchanged from the input. Moreover, in the large <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> regime the angle between input tokens <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>) concentrate near <math id="S3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, so that the simplex Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is effectively satisfied. In this setting, we observe a sharp phase transition in agreement with Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>. In the small <math id="S3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> regime, however, the input tokens <math id="S3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> randomly distributed in an interval <math id="S3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho_{1},\rho_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho_{1},\rho_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and an intermediate phase emerges in which the contraction is only partial: some angles shrink significantly while others remain close to their original values, which smooths out the transition.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F1.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05554v1/phase_diagram_attn_L1_d2_nt1024_ni10.png" id="S3.F1.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:224/186;" width="224" height="186" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F1.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="S3.F1.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F1.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05554v1/phase_diagram_attn_L1_d32_nt1024_ni10.png" id="S3.F1.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:224/186;" width="224" height="186" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F1.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="S3.F1.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=32</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F1.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05554v1/phase_diagram_attn_L1_d512_nt1024_ni10.png" id="S3.F1.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:224/186;" width="224" height="186" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F1.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><math id="S3.F1.sf3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=512</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>. </span><span id="S3.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Plots of the input-to-output angle ratio <math id="S3.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, defined in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 3.2 ‣ 3. Numerical Experiments ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>), as a function of <math id="S3.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. The tokens are first normalized by a pre-layer normalization and then passed through a single self-attention layer (<a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2.2 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>), with residual connections and MLP layers omitted. The dashed curve corresponds to <math id="S3.F1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\tfrac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\tfrac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, which approximates the actual phase transition with increasing accuracy as <math id="S3.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> grows, as implied by Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3. Numerical Experiments ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we plot the normalized matrix norm for the <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nd\times nd" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nd\times nd</annotation></semantics></math> matrix <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as</p>
<table id="S3.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta=\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta=\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">for samples passed through a single self-attention layer with varying <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and dimension <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. Across all three plots, the normalized gradient norm remains close to <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is small, while for large <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> it approaches <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-1/d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-1/d</annotation></semantics></math>, consistent with Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>. Similar to the token-angle behavior, a sharp phase transition emerges near <math id="S3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\tfrac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\tfrac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> in the large-<math id="S3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> regime, in agreement with the predictions under the simplex assumption. In lower dimensions, fluctuations in the pairwise angle prevent perfect concentration, and the transition is smoothed into an intermediate regime where the gradient norm only partially stabilizes.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05554v1/g_phase_diagram_attn_L1_d2_nt1024_ni10.png" id="S3.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:224/186;" width="224" height="186" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="S3.F2.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F2.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05554v1/g_phase_diagram_attn_L1_d32_nt1024_ni10.png" id="S3.F2.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:224/186;" width="224" height="186" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="S3.F2.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=32</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F2.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05554v1/g_phase_diagram_attn_L1_d512_nt1024_ni10.png" id="S3.F2.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:224/186;" width="224" height="186" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><math id="S3.F2.sf3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=512</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>. </span><span id="S3.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Plots of the normalized norm <math id="S3.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> of the gradient, defined by (<a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3.3 ‣ 3. Numerical Experiments ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>), as a function of <math id="S3.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. The tokens are first normalized by a pre-layer normalization and then passed through a single self-attention layer (<a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2.2 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>), with residual connections and MLP layers omitted. The dash curve shows <math id="S3.F2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, which approximate the actual phase transition with increasing accuracy as <math id="S3.F2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> grows, as implied by Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>. The matrix norm <math id="S3.F2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is computed by the Hutchinson trace estimator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hut (89)</a></cite>, based on the definition in (<a href="#S2.E15" title="Equation 2.15 ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.15</span></a>).
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we adopt Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and prove Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> first. Then, we prove Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>. To simplify notations, we define <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket\coloneqq\{1,2,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket\coloneqq\{1,2,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{Z}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{Z}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We study the asymptotics of the quantity <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the notation</p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{i}\coloneqq\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{a_{ik}}=e^{\beta}+\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{i}\coloneqq\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{a_{ik}}=e^{\beta}+\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant. Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>), for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{i}=\begin{cases}(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}$},\\
(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}$},\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{i}=\begin{cases}(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}$},\\
(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}$},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the terms <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> go to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> with speeds independent of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> but only depending on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho_{1},\rho_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho_{1},\rho_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We notice that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{i}=e^{\beta}+\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{i}=e^{\beta}+\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We also notice that <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta t}=n^{\gamma t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta t}=n^{\gamma t}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. It then holds that <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta}=n^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta}=n^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n^{\gamma\rho_{1}}(n-1)\leq\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\leq n^{\gamma\rho_{2}}(n-1)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n^{\gamma\rho_{1}}(n-1)\leq\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\leq n^{\gamma\rho_{2}}(n-1)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, when <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\gamma}&lt;n^{1+\gamma\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\gamma}&lt;n^{1+\gamma\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the leading order term in <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also see that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{i}=\left(\frac{e^{\beta}}{\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)}+1\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{i}=\left(\frac{e^{\beta}}{\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)}+1\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">with</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{e^{\beta}}{\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)}\leq\frac{n^{\gamma}}{n^{\gamma\rho_{1}}(n-1)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{e^{\beta}}{\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)}\leq\frac{n^{\gamma}}{n^{\gamma\rho_{1}}(n-1)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">which goes to <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and is independent of <math id="A1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> but only depending on <math id="A1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, when <math id="A1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\gamma}&gt;n^{1+\gamma\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\gamma}&gt;n^{1+\gamma\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the leading order term in <math id="A1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and similar arguments hold true.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant. Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>), if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=y_{i}+o_{n}(1),\text{ and hence }x_{i}^{\prime}=y_{i}+\alpha x_{i}+o_{n}(1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and hence </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=y_{i}+o_{n}(1),\text{ and hence }x_{i}^{\prime}=y_{i}+\alpha x_{i}+o_{n}(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the term <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> goes to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> with a speed independent of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> but only depending on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we see that when <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\gamma}&gt;n^{1+\gamma\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\gamma}&gt;n^{1+\gamma\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=Z_{i}^{-1}\left(e^{\beta}y_{i}+\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}y_{j}\right)=(1+o_{n}(1))\left(y_{i}+e^{-\beta}\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}y_{j}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=Z_{i}^{-1}\left(e^{\beta}y_{i}+\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}y_{j}\right)=(1+o_{n}(1))\left(y_{i}+e^{-\beta}\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}y_{j}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|y_{j}\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|y_{j}\|=1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|e^{-\beta}\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}y_{j}\right\|\leq e^{-\beta}\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}\leq n^{-\gamma}\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{2}}(n-1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|e^{-\beta}\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}y_{j}\right\|\leq e^{-\beta}\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}\leq n^{-\gamma}\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{2}}(n-1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">which goes to <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and is independent of <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> but only depending on <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This shows that when <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=(1+o_{n}(1))(y_{i}+o_{n}(1))=y_{i}+o_{n}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})=(1+o_{n}(1))(y_{i}+o_{n}(1))=y_{i}+o_{n}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>), for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle&amp;=\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|^{2}+\frac{2\alpha\|x_{i}\|}{Z_{i}}\left(e^{\beta}+\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle\right)\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{1}{Z_{i}^{2}}\left(e^{2\beta}+2e^{\beta}\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle+\sum_{j\neq i}\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ij}+a_{ik}}\langle y_{k},y_{j}\rangle\right).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle&amp;=\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|^{2}+\frac{2\alpha\|x_{i}\|}{Z_{i}}\left(e^{\beta}+\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle\right)\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{1}{Z_{i}^{2}}\left(e^{2\beta}+2e^{\beta}\sum_{j\neq i}e^{a_{ij}}\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle+\sum_{j\neq i}\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ij}+a_{ik}}\langle y_{k},y_{j}\rangle\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant. When <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|^{2}+2\alpha\|x_{i}\|\frac{\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\langle y_{i},y_{k}\rangle}{\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}}+\frac{\sum_{k\neq i}\sum_{l\neq i}e^{a_{ik}+a_{il}}\langle y_{k},y_{l}\rangle}{\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)^{2}}+o_{n}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|^{2}+2\alpha\|x_{i}\|\frac{\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\langle y_{i},y_{k}\rangle}{\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}}+\frac{\sum_{k\neq i}\sum_{l\neq i}e^{a_{ik}+a_{il}}\langle y_{k},y_{l}\rangle}{\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)^{2}}+o_{n}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=(\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1)^{2}+o_{n}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=(\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1)^{2}+o_{n}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In both cases, the terms <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> go to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> with speeds independent of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> but only depending on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho_{1},\rho_{2},\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho_{1},\rho_{2},\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>), we see that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|^{2}+2\alpha\langle x_{i},\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})\rangle+\langle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i}),\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|^{2}+2\alpha\langle x_{i},\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})\rangle+\langle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i}),\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">(<a href="#A1.E11" title="Equation A.11 ‣ Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>) follows from direct computations. Two phase transitions (<a href="#A1.E12" title="Equation A.12 ‣ Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E13" title="Equation A.13 ‣ Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.13</span></a>) follow from similar arguments as in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>), for any two different <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\alpha^{2}\langle x_{i},x_{j}\rangle\\
&amp;+\frac{\alpha\|x_{j}\|}{Z_{i}}\left(e^{\beta}\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle+\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\langle y_{j},y_{k}\rangle\right)+\frac{\alpha\|x_{i}\|}{Z_{j}}\left(e^{\beta}\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle+\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{jl}}\langle y_{i},y_{l}\rangle\right)\\
&amp;+\frac{1}{Z_{i}Z_{j}}\left(e^{2\beta}\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle+e^{\beta}\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\langle y_{j},y_{k}\rangle+e^{\beta}\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{jl}}\langle y_{i},y_{l}\rangle+\sum_{k\neq i}\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{ik}+a_{jl}}\langle y_{k},y_{l}\rangle\right).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\alpha^{2}\langle x_{i},x_{j}\rangle\\
&amp;+\frac{\alpha\|x_{j}\|}{Z_{i}}\left(e^{\beta}\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle+\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\langle y_{j},y_{k}\rangle\right)+\frac{\alpha\|x_{i}\|}{Z_{j}}\left(e^{\beta}\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle+\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{jl}}\langle y_{i},y_{l}\rangle\right)\\
&amp;+\frac{1}{Z_{i}Z_{j}}\left(e^{2\beta}\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle+e^{\beta}\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\langle y_{j},y_{k}\rangle+e^{\beta}\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{jl}}\langle y_{i},y_{l}\rangle+\sum_{k\neq i}\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{ik}+a_{jl}}\langle y_{k},y_{l}\rangle\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant. When <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle&amp;=\alpha^{2}\langle x_{i},x_{j}\rangle+\alpha\|x_{j}\|\frac{\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\langle y_{j},y_{k}\rangle}{\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}}+\alpha\|x_{i}\|\frac{\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{jl}}\langle y_{i},y_{l}\rangle}{\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{jl}}}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{\sum_{k\neq i}\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{ik}+a_{jl}}\langle y_{k},y_{l}\rangle}{\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{jl}}\right)}+o_{n}(1).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle&amp;=\alpha^{2}\langle x_{i},x_{j}\rangle+\alpha\|x_{j}\|\frac{\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\langle y_{j},y_{k}\rangle}{\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}}+\alpha\|x_{i}\|\frac{\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{jl}}\langle y_{i},y_{l}\rangle}{\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{jl}}}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{\sum_{k\neq i}\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{ik}+a_{jl}}\langle y_{k},y_{l}\rangle}{\left(\sum_{k\neq i}e^{a_{ik}}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{l\neq j}e^{a_{jl}}\right)}+o_{n}(1).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=(\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1)(\alpha\|x_{j}\|+1)\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle+o_{n}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=(\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1)(\alpha\|x_{j}\|+1)\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle+o_{n}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>), we see that for two different <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\alpha^{2}p+\alpha\langle x_{i},\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j})\rangle+\alpha\langle x_{j},\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})\rangle+\langle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i}),\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j})\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\alpha^{2}p+\alpha\langle x_{i},\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j})\rangle+\alpha\langle x_{j},\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i})\rangle+\langle\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{i}),\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j})\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">(<a href="#A1.E15" title="Equation A.15 ‣ Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.15</span></a>) follows from direct computations. Two phase transitions (<a href="#A1.E16" title="Equation A.16 ‣ Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.16</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E17" title="Equation A.17 ‣ Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.17</span></a>) follow from similar arguments as in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we prove Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first discuss the case when <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. According to (<a href="#A1.E16" title="Equation A.16 ‣ Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.16</span></a>) and Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we see that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle&amp;\geq\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|\|x_{j}\|\rho_{1}+\alpha\|x_{j}\|\rho_{1}+\alpha\|x_{i}\|\rho_{1}+\rho_{1}+o_{n}(1)\\
&amp;=\rho_{1}(\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1)(\alpha\|x_{j}\|+1)+o_{n}(1).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle&amp;\geq\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|\|x_{j}\|\rho_{1}+\alpha\|x_{j}\|\rho_{1}+\alpha\|x_{i}\|\rho_{1}+\rho_{1}+o_{n}(1)\\
&amp;=\rho_{1}(\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1)(\alpha\|x_{j}\|+1)+o_{n}(1).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#A1.E12" title="Equation A.12 ‣ Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>), we see that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle&amp;\leq\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|^{2}+2\alpha\|x_{i}\|\rho_{2}+\rho_{2}+o_{n}(1)\\
&amp;=\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|^{2}+2\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1-(1-\rho_{2})(1+2\alpha\|x_{i}\|)+o_{n}(1)\\
&amp;\leq(\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1)^{2}-(1-\rho_{2})(1+2\alpha q_{1})+o_{n}(1).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle&amp;\leq\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|^{2}+2\alpha\|x_{i}\|\rho_{2}+\rho_{2}+o_{n}(1)\\
&amp;=\alpha^{2}\|x_{i}\|^{2}+2\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1-(1-\rho_{2})(1+2\alpha\|x_{i}\|)+o_{n}(1)\\
&amp;\leq(\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1)^{2}-(1-\rho_{2})(1+2\alpha q_{1})+o_{n}(1).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">We have a similar inequality for <math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{j}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{j}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. So, there is a constant <math id="A1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> depending on <math id="A1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{2},\alpha,q_{1},q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{2},\alpha,q_{1},q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and independent of <math id="A1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\|x_{i}^{\prime}\|}\geq\frac{1+\delta}{\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1}+o_{n}(1),\text{ and }\frac{1}{\|x_{j}^{\prime}\|}\geq\frac{1+\delta}{\alpha\|x_{j}\|+1}+o_{n}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\|x_{i}^{\prime}\|}\geq\frac{1+\delta}{\alpha\|x_{i}\|+1}+o_{n}(1),\text{ and }\frac{1}{\|x_{j}^{\prime}\|}\geq\frac{1+\delta}{\alpha\|x_{j}\|+1}+o_{n}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle\geq\rho_{1}(1+\delta)^{2}+o_{n}(1)\geq\rho_{1}+\varepsilon+o_{n}(1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle\geq\rho_{1}(1+\delta)^{2}+o_{n}(1)\geq\rho_{1}+\varepsilon+o_{n}(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=\rho_{1}(1+2\delta)\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=\rho_{1}(1+2\delta)\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> independent of <math id="A1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the case when <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#S2.E9" title="Equation 2.9 ‣ Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.9</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E10" title="Equation 2.10 ‣ Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>) follow directly from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, and Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We notice that Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> corresponds to the special case when <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}=q_{2}=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}=q_{2}=q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{1}=\rho_{2}=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{1}=\rho_{2}=\rho</annotation></semantics></math> in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Clearly, <math id="A1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of the choice of <math id="A1.p10.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> by its definition (<a href="#A1.E1" title="Equation A.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>). According to the explicit forms (<a href="#A1.E11" title="Equation A.11 ‣ Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>) in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> and (<a href="#A1.E15" title="Equation A.15 ‣ Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.15</span></a>) in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, one directly sees that both <math id="A1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i},x_{i}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i},x_{i}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x_{i},x_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{i},x_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> are independent of the choices of <math id="A1.p10.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>. We can further compute that
for any <math id="A1.p10.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=\begin{cases}\alpha^{2}q+2\alpha\sqrt{q}\rho+\rho&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\alpha^{2}q+\alpha\sqrt{q}(1+\rho)+\frac{1+3\rho}{4}&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{i}^{\prime}\rangle=\begin{cases}\alpha^{2}q+2\alpha\sqrt{q}\rho+\rho&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\alpha^{2}q+\alpha\sqrt{q}(1+\rho)+\frac{1+3\rho}{4}&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">and for any two different <math id="A1.p10.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\rho(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle x_{i}^{\prime},x_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\rho(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">(<a href="#S2.E4" title="Equation 2.4 ‣ Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>) follows from (<a href="#A1.E23" title="Equation A.23 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.23</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E24" title="Equation A.24 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.24</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(A.25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\frac{\rho(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}}{\alpha^{2}q+2\alpha\sqrt{q}\rho+\rho}&gt;\frac{\rho(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}}{\alpha^{2}q+2\alpha\sqrt{q}+1}=\rho," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle=\frac{\rho(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}}{\alpha^{2}q+2\alpha\sqrt{q}\rho+\rho}&gt;\frac{\rho(\alpha\sqrt{q}+1)^{2}}{\alpha^{2}q+2\alpha\sqrt{q}+1}=\rho,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the strict inequality is because <math id="A1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can similarly show that <math id="A1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle&gt;\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{n\to+\infty}\langle y_{i}^{\prime},y_{j}^{\prime}\rangle&gt;\rho</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof for Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a> first. We need to explicitly compute terms in <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for which we need the following lemmas.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1. </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,k\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,k\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u,w\in\llbracket 1,d\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,w\in\llbracket 1,d\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial(N(x_{k}))_{w}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}=\delta_{ik}\frac{\delta_{wu}\|x_{k}\|^{2}-(x_{k})_{w}(x_{k})_{u}}{\|x_{k}\|^{3}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial(N(x_{k}))_{w}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}=\delta_{ik}\frac{\delta_{wu}\|x_{k}\|^{2}-(x_{k})_{w}(x_{k})_{u}}{\|x_{k}\|^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial(N(x_{k}))_{w}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}=\frac{\partial((x_{k})_{w}\cdot\|x_{k}\|^{-1})}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}=\delta_{ik}\frac{\delta_{wu}\|x_{k}\|-(x_{k})_{w}\cdot\frac{(x_{k})_{u}}{\|x_{k}\|}}{\|x_{k}\|^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial(N(x_{k}))_{w}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}=\frac{\partial((x_{k})_{w}\cdot\|x_{k}\|^{-1})}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}=\delta_{ik}\frac{\delta_{wu}\|x_{k}\|-(x_{k})_{w}\cdot\frac{(x_{k})_{u}}{\|x_{k}\|}}{\|x_{k}\|^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w,v\in\llbracket 1,d\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w,v\in\llbracket 1,d\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{k})_{w}}\\
&amp;=\bigg[\left(\delta_{kj}\beta\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m})_{w}(y_{m})_{v}\right)+e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{k}\rangle}(\beta(y_{j})_{w}(y_{k})_{v}+\delta_{wv})\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}\right)\\
&amp;\quad-\left(\delta_{kj}\beta\left(\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}(y_{l})_{w}\right)+\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{k}\rangle}(y_{j})_{w}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m})_{v}\right)\bigg]\\
&amp;\quad\cdot\left(\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}\right)^{-2}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{k})_{w}}\\
&amp;=\bigg[\left(\delta_{kj}\beta\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m})_{w}(y_{m})_{v}\right)+e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{k}\rangle}(\beta(y_{j})_{w}(y_{k})_{v}+\delta_{wv})\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}\right)\\
&amp;\quad-\left(\delta_{kj}\beta\left(\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}(y_{l})_{w}\right)+\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{k}\rangle}(y_{j})_{w}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m})_{v}\right)\bigg]\\
&amp;\quad\cdot\left(\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}\right)^{-2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2.2 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}=\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m})_{v}}{\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}=\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m})_{v}}{\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> then follows from a direct computation.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.338em;" width="0.338em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\otimes y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\otimes y</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> matrix with <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math>-th element <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x\otimes y)_{uv}=(x)_{u}(y)_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x\otimes y)_{uv}=(x)_{u}(y)_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\otimes y\coloneqq xy^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\otimes y\coloneqq xy^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then have the following proposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Adopt Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>).
For any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> matrix formed by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u,v\in\llbracket 1,d\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in\llbracket 1,d\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}=N(x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}=N(x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, this matrix has the following form:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{d\times d}=\|x_{i}\|^{-\frac{1}{2}}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})Z_{j}-(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{d\times d}=\|x_{i}\|^{-\frac{1}{2}}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})Z_{j}-(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}=\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}=\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#A1.E1" title="Equation A.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{R}_{1}\coloneqq\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{W}_{j}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{j}y_{i})\right),\quad\mathbf{R}_{2}\coloneqq e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{R}_{1}\coloneqq\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{W}_{j}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{j}y_{i})\right),\quad\mathbf{R}_{2}\coloneqq e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbf{U}_{1}\coloneqq\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}_{j}\right),\quad\mathbf{U}_{2}\coloneqq\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbf{U}_{1}\coloneqq\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}_{j}\right),\quad\mathbf{U}_{2}\coloneqq\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In (<a href="#A2.E6" title="Equation B.6 ‣ Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E7" title="Equation B.7 ‣ Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{V}_{j}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}y_{m},\quad\mathbf{W}_{j}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}y_{m}\otimes y_{m},\quad\mathbf{P}_{x}y\coloneqq y-\langle y,x\rangle x." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{V}_{j}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}y_{m},\quad\mathbf{W}_{j}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}y_{m}\otimes y_{m},\quad\mathbf{P}_{x}y\coloneqq y-\langle y,x\rangle x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By chain rule and Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\\
&amp;=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\sum_{w=1}^{d}\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{k})_{w}}\bigg|_{Y=\mathcal{N}(X)}\cdot\frac{\partial(N(x_{k}))_{w}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\\
&amp;=\|x_{i}\|^{-\frac{3}{2}}\left(\|x_{i}\|\cdot\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{u}}-\sum_{w=1}^{d}(x_{i})_{u}(x_{i})_{w}\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{w}}\right)\bigg|_{Y=\mathcal{N}(X)}\\
&amp;=\|x_{i}\|^{-\frac{1}{2}}\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{u}}-(y_{i})_{u}\sum_{w=1}^{d}(y_{i})_{w}\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{w}}\right)\bigg|_{Y=\mathcal{N}(X)}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\\
&amp;=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\sum_{w=1}^{d}\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{k})_{w}}\bigg|_{Y=\mathcal{N}(X)}\cdot\frac{\partial(N(x_{k}))_{w}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\\
&amp;=\|x_{i}\|^{-\frac{3}{2}}\left(\|x_{i}\|\cdot\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{u}}-\sum_{w=1}^{d}(x_{i})_{u}(x_{i})_{w}\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{w}}\right)\bigg|_{Y=\mathcal{N}(X)}\\
&amp;=\|x_{i}\|^{-\frac{1}{2}}\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{u}}-(y_{i})_{u}\sum_{w=1}^{d}(y_{i})_{w}\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{w}}\right)\bigg|_{Y=\mathcal{N}(X)}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">According to Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> and the notation <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}=\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{a_{jl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}=\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{a_{jl}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{w=1}^{d}(y_{i})_{w}\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{w}}\\
&amp;=\bigg[\left(\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle(y_{m})_{v}\right)+e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}(\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle+1)(y_{i})_{v}\right)\cdot Z_{j}\\
&amp;\quad-\left(\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}\langle y_{l},y_{i}\rangle\right)+\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m})_{v}\right)\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{w=1}^{d}(y_{i})_{w}\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{w}}\\
&amp;=\bigg[\left(\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle(y_{m})_{v}\right)+e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}(\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle+1)(y_{i})_{v}\right)\cdot Z_{j}\\
&amp;\quad-\left(\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}\langle y_{l},y_{i}\rangle\right)+\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m})_{v}\right)\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\|x_{i}\|^{\frac{1}{2}}\cdot\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\\
&amp;=\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{u}}-(y_{i})_{u}\sum_{w=1}^{d}(y_{i})_{w}\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{w}}\right)\bigg|_{Y=\mathcal{N}(X)}\\
&amp;=\bigg[\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}\left((y_{m})_{u}(y_{m})_{v}-\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle(y_{m})_{v}(y_{i})_{u}\right)\right)\\
&amp;\quad+e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}(\beta(y_{j})_{u}(y_{i})_{v}+\delta_{uv}-\left(\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle+1\right)(y_{i})_{v}(y_{i})_{u})\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}\\
&amp;\quad-\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}\left((y_{l})_{u}-\langle y_{l},y_{i}\rangle(y_{i})_{u}\right)\right)\\
&amp;\quad+\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left((y_{j})_{u}-\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle(y_{i})_{u}\right)\bigg]\cdot\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m})_{v}\right)\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\|x_{i}\|^{\frac{1}{2}}\cdot\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\\
&amp;=\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{u}}-(y_{i})_{u}\sum_{w=1}^{d}(y_{i})_{w}\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(y_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(y_{i})_{w}}\right)\bigg|_{Y=\mathcal{N}(X)}\\
&amp;=\bigg[\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}\left((y_{m})_{u}(y_{m})_{v}-\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle(y_{m})_{v}(y_{i})_{u}\right)\right)\\
&amp;\quad+e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}(\beta(y_{j})_{u}(y_{i})_{v}+\delta_{uv}-\left(\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle+1\right)(y_{i})_{v}(y_{i})_{u})\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}\\
&amp;\quad-\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\sum_{l=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{l}\rangle}\left((y_{l})_{u}-\langle y_{l},y_{i}\rangle(y_{i})_{u}\right)\right)\\
&amp;\quad+\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left((y_{j})_{u}-\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle(y_{i})_{u}\right)\bigg]\cdot\left(\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m})_{v}\right)\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">We then adopt the notation (<a href="#A2.E8" title="Equation B.8 ‣ Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>), i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{V}_{j}=\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}y_{m},\quad\mathbf{W}_{j}=\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}y_{m}\otimes y_{m},\quad\mathbf{P}_{x}y\coloneqq y-\langle y,x\rangle x." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{V}_{j}=\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}y_{m},\quad\mathbf{W}_{j}=\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}y_{m}\otimes y_{m},\quad\mathbf{P}_{x}y\coloneqq y-\langle y,x\rangle x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">So, the matrix form of (<a href="#A2.E11" title="Equation B.11 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a>) becomes</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\bigg[\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{W}_{j}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{j}y_{i})\right)+e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}(\beta y_{j}\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}-\left(\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle+1\right)y_{i}\otimes y_{i})\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}\\
&amp;-\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{V}_{j}-\langle\mathbf{V}_{j},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\right)+\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(y_{j}-\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\right)\bigg]\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}\\
&amp;=\bigg[\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{W}_{j}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{j}y_{i})\right)+e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d})\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}\\
&amp;-\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}_{j}\right)+\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)\bigg]\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\bigg[\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{W}_{j}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{j}y_{i})\right)+e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}(\beta y_{j}\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}-\left(\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle+1\right)y_{i}\otimes y_{i})\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}\\
&amp;-\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{V}_{j}-\langle\mathbf{V}_{j},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\right)+\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(y_{j}-\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\right)\bigg]\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}\\
&amp;=\bigg[\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{W}_{j}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{j}y_{i})\right)+e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d})\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}\\
&amp;-\bigg[\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}_{j}\right)+\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)\bigg]\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\bigg]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">We further use the notations in (<a href="#A2.E6" title="Equation B.6 ‣ Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E7" title="Equation B.7 ‣ Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>), i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{R}_{1}=\delta_{ij}\beta e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{W}_{j}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{j}y_{i})\right),\quad\mathbf{R}_{2}=e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{R}_{1}=\delta_{ij}\beta e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{W}_{j}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{j}y_{i})\right),\quad\mathbf{R}_{2}=e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbf{U}_{1}=\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}_{j}\right),\quad\mathbf{U}_{2}=\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbf{U}_{1}=\delta_{ij}\beta\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}_{j}\right),\quad\mathbf{U}_{2}=\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, the matrix form of (<a href="#A2.E11" title="Equation B.11 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a>) becomes</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})Z-(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})Z-(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant. Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>), if <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any fixed <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> matrix satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{d\times d}=\frac{\delta_{ij}}{\|x_{i}\|}\left(I_{d}-y_{i}\otimes y_{i}\right)+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)+o_{n}(1)\cdot I_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{d\times d}=\frac{\delta_{ij}}{\|x_{i}\|}\left(I_{d}-y_{i}\otimes y_{i}\right)+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)+o_{n}(1)\cdot I_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the leading order term is exactly <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial(N(x_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial(N(x_{j}))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The term <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively) is a <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> matrix (constant, respectively) with matrix norm as defined in (<a href="#S2.E15" title="Equation 2.15 ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.15</span></a>) (value, respectively) going to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, with a speed independent of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math> but only depending on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho_{2},q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho_{2},q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We frequently use this formula: for two vectors <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1},V_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1},V_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the matrix norm of <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1}\otimes V_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1}\otimes V_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in (<a href="#S2.E15" title="Equation 2.15 ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.15</span></a>) is <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|V_{1}\|\|V_{2}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|V_{1}\|\|V_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\gamma}&gt;n^{1+\gamma\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\gamma}&gt;n^{1+\gamma\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we know from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> that <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}=(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}=(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>. Adopt the notations in Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, we then show the following facts when <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{R}_{1}Z_{j}^{-1}=\mathbf{o}_{n}(1),\quad\mathbf{R}_{2}Z_{j}^{-1}=\delta_{ij}\left(-y_{i}\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)+o_{n}(1)\cdot I_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{R}_{1}Z_{j}^{-1}=\mathbf{o}_{n}(1),\quad\mathbf{R}_{2}Z_{j}^{-1}=\delta_{ij}\left(-y_{i}\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)+o_{n}(1)\cdot I_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}=\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}=\mathbf{o}_{n}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, for <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{1}Z_{j}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{1}Z_{j}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, when <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math> by its definition. When <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{1}=\beta\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\left(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{1}=\beta\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\left(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and we notice that the term when <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=i</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. So, because <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\|\leq\|y_{m}\|^{2}+\|y_{m}\|^{2}\|y_{i}\|^{2}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\|\leq\|y_{m}\|^{2}+\|y_{m}\|^{2}\|y_{i}\|^{2}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta}=n^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta}=n^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{R}_{1}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\beta(n-1)e^{\beta\rho_{2}}\cdot 2Z_{j}^{-1}\leq 2\gamma\log(n)\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{2}+1-\gamma}(1+o_{n}(1))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{R}_{1}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\beta(n-1)e^{\beta\rho_{2}}\cdot 2Z_{j}^{-1}\leq 2\gamma\log(n)\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{2}+1-\gamma}(1+o_{n}(1)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">which goes to <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> with a speed independent of <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\rho_{2}+1-\gamma&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\rho_{2}+1-\gamma&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{2}Z_{j}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{2}Z_{j}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we notice that when <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle}Z_{j}^{-1}\leq e^{\beta(\rho_{2}-1)}(1+o_{n}(1))=n^{\gamma(\rho_{2}-1)}(1+o_{n}(1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle}Z_{j}^{-1}\leq e^{\beta(\rho_{2}-1)}(1+o_{n}(1))=n^{\gamma(\rho_{2}-1)}(1+o_{n}(1))</annotation></semantics></math>, which goes to <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> with a speed independent of <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>. So, <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{2}Z_{j}^{-1}=\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)+o_{n}(1)\cdot I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{2}Z_{j}^{-1}=\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)+o_{n}(1)\cdot I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{2}=e^{\beta}\left(-y_{i}\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{2}=e^{\beta}\left(-y_{i}\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and so <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{2}Z_{j}^{-1}=(-y_{i}\otimes y_{i}+I_{d})+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)+o_{n}(1)\cdot I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{2}Z_{j}^{-1}=(-y_{i}\otimes y_{i}+I_{d})+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)+o_{n}(1)\cdot I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that when <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and so</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\left\|(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right\|\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}\leq Z_{j}^{-2}\beta\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}+y_{i}\rangle}\|y_{m}\|\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|\\
&amp;\leq Z_{j}^{-2}\beta e^{\beta(1+\rho_{2})}n=\gamma\log(n)n^{\gamma(\rho_{2}-1)+1}(1+o_{n}(1)),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\left\|(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right\|\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}\leq Z_{j}^{-2}\beta\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}+y_{i}\rangle}\|y_{m}\|\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|\\
&amp;\leq Z_{j}^{-2}\beta e^{\beta(1+\rho_{2})}n=\gamma\log(n)n^{\gamma(\rho_{2}-1)+1}(1+o_{n}(1)),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">which goes to <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> with a speed independent of <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and so</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\left\|(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right\|\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}\leq Z_{j}^{-2}\beta\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}_{i}\|\|\mathbf{V}_{i}\|\\
&amp;\leq Z_{j}^{-2}\beta\left(\sum_{m\neq i}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{m}\|\right)\cdot\left(e^{\beta}+\sum_{m\neq i}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{m}\|\right)\\
&amp;\leq Z_{j}^{-2}\beta\left(e^{\beta\rho_{2}}n\right)\cdot\left(e^{\beta}+e^{\beta\rho_{2}}n\right)\\
&amp;=\gamma\log(n)n^{\gamma(\rho_{2}-1)+1}(1+n^{\gamma(\rho_{2}-1)+1})(1+o_{n}(1)),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\left\|(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right\|\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}\leq Z_{j}^{-2}\beta\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}_{i}\|\|\mathbf{V}_{i}\|\\
&amp;\leq Z_{j}^{-2}\beta\left(\sum_{m\neq i}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{m}\|\right)\cdot\left(e^{\beta}+\sum_{m\neq i}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{m}\|\right)\\
&amp;\leq Z_{j}^{-2}\beta\left(e^{\beta\rho_{2}}n\right)\cdot\left(e^{\beta}+e^{\beta\rho_{2}}n\right)\\
&amp;=\gamma\log(n)n^{\gamma(\rho_{2}-1)+1}(1+n^{\gamma(\rho_{2}-1)+1})(1+o_{n}(1)),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">which goes to <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> with a speed independent of <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}=\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}=\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant. Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>), if <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for fixed <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> matrix satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{d\times d}\right\|\leq\|x_{i}\|^{-\frac{1}{2}}\cdot\left(2\beta\delta_{ij}+(2\beta+\sqrt{d})e^{a_{ij}}Z_{j}^{-1}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{d\times d}\right\|\leq\|x_{i}\|^{-\frac{1}{2}}\cdot\left(2\beta\delta_{ij}+(2\beta+\sqrt{d})e^{a_{ij}}Z_{j}^{-1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma B.5. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, when <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}=(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot\left(\sum_{k\neq j}e^{a_{jk}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}=(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot\left(\sum_{k\neq j}e^{a_{jk}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}\geq n^{\gamma\rho_{1}+1}(1+o_{n}(1))&gt;n^{\gamma}(1+o_{n}(1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}\geq n^{\gamma\rho_{1}+1}(1+o_{n}(1))&gt;n^{\gamma}(1+o_{n}(1))</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\rho_{1}+1&gt;\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\rho_{1}+1&gt;\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Adopt the notations in Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, we then show the following facts when <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{R}_{1}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\delta_{ij}\beta,\quad\|\mathbf{R}_{2}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq Z_{j}^{-1}e^{a_{ij}}\left(\beta+\sqrt{d-1}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{R}_{1}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\delta_{ij}\beta,\quad\|\mathbf{R}_{2}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq Z_{j}^{-1}e^{a_{ij}}\left(\beta+\sqrt{d-1}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right\|\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}\leq\beta\left(\delta_{ij}+e^{a_{ij}}Z_{j}^{-1}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right\|\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}\leq\beta\left(\delta_{ij}+e^{a_{ij}}Z_{j}^{-1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, for <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{1}Z_{j}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{1}Z_{j}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, when <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math> by its definition. When <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{1}=\beta\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\left(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{1}=\beta\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\left(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. So, because we have that <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\|=\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{n}\otimes y_{m}\|=\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{n}\|\|y_{m}\|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\|=\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{n}\otimes y_{m}\|=\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{n}\|\|y_{m}\|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{R}_{1}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\beta Z_{j}\cdot\cdot Z_{j}^{-1}=\beta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐑</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{R}_{1}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\beta Z_{j}\cdot\cdot Z_{j}^{-1}=\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{2}Z_{j}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{2}Z_{j}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|-y_{i}\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\|=\sqrt{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|-y_{i}\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\|=\sqrt{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\|\mathbf{R}_{2}\|Z_{j}^{-1}&amp;\leq Z_{j}^{-1}e^{a_{ij}}\left(\beta+\sqrt{d-1}\right).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\|\mathbf{R}_{2}\|Z_{j}^{-1}&amp;\leq Z_{j}^{-1}e^{a_{ij}}\left(\beta+\sqrt{d-1}\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A2.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right]\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that <math id="A2.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{V}_{j}\|\leq\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}=Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{V}_{j}\|\leq\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle}=Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, <math id="A2.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{U}_{1}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\delta_{ij}\beta\|\mathbf{V}_{j}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\delta_{ij}\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{U}_{1}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\delta_{ij}\beta\|\mathbf{V}_{j}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\delta_{ij}\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{U}_{2}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\beta e^{a_{ij}}Z_{j}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{U}_{2}\|Z_{j}^{-1}\leq\beta e^{a_{ij}}Z_{j}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.28)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right\|\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}\leq\beta\left(\delta_{ij}+e^{a_{ij}}Z_{j}^{-1}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes\mathbf{V}_{j}\right\|\cdot Z_{j}^{-2}\leq\beta\left(\delta_{ij}+e^{a_{ij}}Z_{j}^{-1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a> follows directly from Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma B.5. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2. </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof for Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> requires more delicate arguments. The part when <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> directly follows from Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, so we only focus on the part when <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\leq\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\leq\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>. We remark that when <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, our result is that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=0+o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=0+o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a better estimate than (<a href="#S2.E20" title="Equation 2.20 ‣ Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.20</span></a>) in Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first have the following lemma which replaces Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> when we adopt Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Adopt Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>).
For any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> matrix formed by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u,v\in\llbracket 1,d\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in\llbracket 1,d\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}=N(x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}=N(x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, this matrix has the following form:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{d\times d}=q^{-\frac{1}{2}}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})Z-(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes(\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4})\right]\cdot Z^{-2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝖠𝖳𝖳</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{\partial(\mathsf{\mathop{ATT}}(N(x_{j})))_{v}}{\partial(x_{i})_{u}}\right)_{d\times d}=q^{-\frac{1}{2}}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})Z-(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})\otimes(\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4})\right]\cdot Z^{-2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=e^{\beta}+(n-1)e^{\beta\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=e^{\beta}+(n-1)e^{\beta\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.30)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{R}_{1}\coloneqq\delta_{ij}\beta e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{W}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}y_{i})\right),\quad\mathbf{R}_{2}\coloneqq e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{R}_{1}\coloneqq\delta_{ij}\beta e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{W}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}y_{i})\right),\quad\mathbf{R}_{2}\coloneqq e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.31)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbf{U}_{1}\coloneqq\delta_{ij}\beta e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right),\quad\mathbf{U}_{2}\coloneqq\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right),\\
&amp;\mathbf{U}_{3}\coloneqq(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})y_{j},\quad\mathbf{U}_{4}\coloneqq e^{\beta\rho}\mathbf{V}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbf{U}_{1}\coloneqq\delta_{ij}\beta e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right),\quad\mathbf{U}_{2}\coloneqq\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right),\\
&amp;\mathbf{U}_{3}\coloneqq(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})y_{j},\quad\mathbf{U}_{4}\coloneqq e^{\beta\rho}\mathbf{V}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In (<a href="#A2.E30" title="Equation B.30 ‣ Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.30</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E31" title="Equation B.31 ‣ Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.31</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.32)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{V}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}y_{m},\quad\mathbf{W}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}y_{m}\otimes y_{m},\quad\mathbf{P}_{x}y\coloneqq y-\langle y,x\rangle x." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{V}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}y_{m},\quad\mathbf{W}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}y_{m}\otimes y_{m},\quad\mathbf{P}_{x}y\coloneqq y-\langle y,x\rangle x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first apply Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> to get (<a href="#A2.E5" title="Equation B.5 ‣ Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>). After replacing <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{j},y_{m}\rangle=\rho</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, we can obtain (<a href="#A2.E29" title="Equation B.29 ‣ Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.29</span></a>). The only remark is that the term <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}(\mathbf{W}_{j}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{j}y_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}(\mathbf{W}_{j}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{j}y_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#A2.E6" title="Equation B.6 ‣ Lemma B.3. ‣ B.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>) is nonzero when <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=j</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, when <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{i}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{i}y_{i})=\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{i}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{i}y_{i})=\sum_{m=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle)</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=i</annotation></semantics></math>, the summand <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle)</annotation></semantics></math> becomes <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{i}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{i}y_{i})=\sum_{m\neq i}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle)=e^{\beta\rho}\sum_{m\neq i}(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle)=e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{W}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}y_{i})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{i}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}_{i}y_{i})=\sum_{m\neq i}e^{\beta\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle)=e^{\beta\rho}\sum_{m\neq i}(y_{m}\otimes y_{m}-y_{i}\otimes y_{m}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle)=e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{W}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}y_{i})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Next, to compute the matrix norm of (<a href="#A2.E29" title="Equation B.29 ‣ Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.29</span></a>), we see that for any matrix <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, its matrix norm square equals to <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tr}(K^{T}K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tr}(K^{T}K)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the matrix norm square of (<a href="#A2.E29" title="Equation B.29 ‣ Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.29</span></a>) equals to</p>
<table id="A2.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.33)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;q^{-1}Z^{-4}\cdot\bigg(\mathrm{Tr}\left[Z^{2}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})\right]-2Z(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})(\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4})\\
&amp;+\|\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}\bigg).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;q^{-1}Z^{-4}\cdot\bigg(\mathrm{Tr}\left[Z^{2}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})\right]-2Z(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})(\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4})\\
&amp;+\|\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}\bigg).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">We then compute these terms separately, and sum them in <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>. We first have the following basic equalities for the notations <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V},\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V},\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.E32" title="Equation B.32 ‣ Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.32</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.7</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the notations in (<a href="#A2.E32" title="Equation B.32 ‣ Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.32</span></a>), i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.34)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{V}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}y_{m},\quad\mathbf{W}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}y_{m}\otimes y_{m},\quad\mathbf{P}_{x}y\coloneqq y-\langle y,x\rangle x," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{V}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}y_{m},\quad\mathbf{W}\coloneqq\sum_{m=1}^{n}y_{m}\otimes y_{m},\quad\mathbf{P}_{x}y\coloneqq y-\langle y,x\rangle x,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.35)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathrm{Tr}(\mathbf{W}^{2})=\sum_{m,l}\langle y_{m},y_{l}\rangle^{2}=n(n\rho^{2}+(1-\rho^{2})),\\
&amp;\mathrm{Tr}(\mathbf{W})=n,\quad\mathrm{Tr}(\mathbf{W}y_{i}y_{i}^{T})=n\rho^{2}+(1-\rho^{2}),\quad\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}=1-\rho^{2}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathrm{Tr}(\mathbf{W}^{2})=\sum_{m,l}\langle y_{m},y_{l}\rangle^{2}=n(n\rho^{2}+(1-\rho^{2})),\\
&amp;\mathrm{Tr}(\mathbf{W})=n,\quad\mathrm{Tr}(\mathbf{W}y_{i}y_{i}^{T})=n\rho^{2}+(1-\rho^{2}),\quad\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}=1-\rho^{2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Also,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.36)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbf{W}y_{i}=\sum_{m=1}^{n}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle y_{m}=(1-\rho)y_{i}+\rho\mathbf{V},\\
&amp;\langle\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle=\sum_{m=1}^{n}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle=n\rho+(1-\rho),\\
&amp;\|\mathbf{V}\|^{2}=\sum_{m,l}\langle y_{m},y_{l}\rangle=n+\rho n(n-1)=n(n\rho+(1-\rho)),\\
&amp;\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{V}\|^{2}-\langle\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle^{2}=(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho),\\
&amp;\|\mathbf{W}y_{i}\|^{2}=n^{2}\rho^{3}+3n\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+(1+2\rho)(1-\rho)^{2}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbf{W}y_{i}=\sum_{m=1}^{n}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle y_{m}=(1-\rho)y_{i}+\rho\mathbf{V},\\
&amp;\langle\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle=\sum_{m=1}^{n}\langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle=n\rho+(1-\rho),\\
&amp;\|\mathbf{V}\|^{2}=\sum_{m,l}\langle y_{m},y_{l}\rangle=n+\rho n(n-1)=n(n\rho+(1-\rho)),\\
&amp;\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{V}\|^{2}-\langle\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle^{2}=(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho),\\
&amp;\|\mathbf{W}y_{i}\|^{2}=n^{2}\rho^{3}+3n\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+(1+2\rho)(1-\rho)^{2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma B.7. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Direct Computations.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.8</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For terms <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{1},\mathbf{R}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{1},\mathbf{R}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.37)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})\right]\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n\left[n^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+n(1-\rho)(1+\rho-3\rho^{2})-(1+2\rho)(1-\rho)^{2}\right]\\
&amp;+\beta e^{\beta(\rho+1)}n(n-1)(1-\rho^{2})\\
&amp;+e^{2\beta}(d-1)n+e^{2\beta\rho}\left[\beta^{2}(1-\rho^{2})+d-1\right]n(n-1).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})\right]\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n\left[n^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+n(1-\rho)(1+\rho-3\rho^{2})-(1+2\rho)(1-\rho)^{2}\right]\\
&amp;+\beta e^{\beta(\rho+1)}n(n-1)(1-\rho^{2})\\
&amp;+e^{2\beta}(d-1)n+e^{2\beta\rho}\left[\beta^{2}(1-\rho^{2})+d-1\right]n(n-1).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As a corollary, when we pick <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following phase transition limits as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.38)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nZ^{2}}\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})\right]=\begin{cases}\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{d-1+\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)}{4}+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
d-1+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nZ^{2}}\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})\right]=\begin{cases}\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{d-1+\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)}{4}+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
d-1+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first notice that <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math> is a symmetric matrix and <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|y_{i}\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|y_{i}\|=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then expand each term in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a> and use Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma B.7. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.39)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1})^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}\right]\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}\sum_{i}\left(\mathrm{Tr}\left(\mathbf{W}^{2}-2\mathbf{W}y_{i}(\mathbf{W}y_{i})^{T}\right)+\|y_{i}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{W}y_{i}\|^{2}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}\sum_{i}\left(\mathrm{Tr}\mathbf{W}^{2}-2\|\mathbf{W}y_{i}\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{W}y_{i}\|^{2}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n\left[n^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+n(1-\rho)(1+\rho-3\rho^{2})-(1+2\rho)(1-\rho)^{2}\right].\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1})^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}\right]\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}\sum_{i}\left(\mathrm{Tr}\left(\mathbf{W}^{2}-2\mathbf{W}y_{i}(\mathbf{W}y_{i})^{T}\right)+\|y_{i}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{W}y_{i}\|^{2}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}\sum_{i}\left(\mathrm{Tr}\mathbf{W}^{2}-2\|\mathbf{W}y_{i}\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{W}y_{i}\|^{2}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n\left[n^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+n(1-\rho)(1+\rho-3\rho^{2})-(1+2\rho)(1-\rho)^{2}\right].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.40)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1})^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\right]\\
&amp;=\mathrm{Tr}\sum_{i,j}\delta_{ij}\beta e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{W}-\mathbf{W}y_{i}y_{i}^{T}\right)e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta e^{\beta(\rho+1)}\mathrm{Tr}\sum_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}-\mathbf{W}y_{i}y_{i}^{T}\right)(-y_{i}y_{i}^{T}+I_{d})=\beta e^{\beta(\rho+1)}\mathrm{Tr}\sum_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}-\mathbf{W}y_{i}y_{i}^{T}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta e^{\beta(\rho+1)}n(n-1)(1-\rho^{2}),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{1})^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\right]\\
&amp;=\mathrm{Tr}\sum_{i,j}\delta_{ij}\beta e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{W}-\mathbf{W}y_{i}y_{i}^{T}\right)e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta e^{\beta(\rho+1)}\mathrm{Tr}\sum_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}-\mathbf{W}y_{i}y_{i}^{T}\right)(-y_{i}y_{i}^{T}+I_{d})=\beta e^{\beta(\rho+1)}\mathrm{Tr}\sum_{i}\left(\mathbf{W}-\mathbf{W}y_{i}y_{i}^{T}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta e^{\beta(\rho+1)}n(n-1)(1-\rho^{2}),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality is because <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.41)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{2})^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\right]\\
&amp;=\sum_{i,j}e^{2\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})y_{i}^{T}+I_{d}\right)\left(y_{i}(-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})^{T}+I_{d}\right]\\
&amp;=\sum_{i\neq j}e^{2\beta\rho}\left[\left(1+\beta^{2}(1-\rho^{2})\right)-2+d\right]+\sum_{i}e^{2\beta}(d-1)\\
&amp;=e^{2\beta}(d-1)n+e^{2\beta\rho}\left[\beta^{2}(1-\rho^{2})+d-1\right]n(n-1).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>Tr</mi><mo>[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(\mathbf{R}_{2})^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\right]\\
&amp;=\sum_{i,j}e^{2\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\mathrm{Tr}\left[(-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})y_{i}^{T}+I_{d}\right)\left(y_{i}(-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})^{T}+I_{d}\right]\\
&amp;=\sum_{i\neq j}e^{2\beta\rho}\left[\left(1+\beta^{2}(1-\rho^{2})\right)-2+d\right]+\sum_{i}e^{2\beta}(d-1)\\
&amp;=e^{2\beta}(d-1)n+e^{2\beta\rho}\left[\beta^{2}(1-\rho^{2})+d-1\right]n(n-1).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we show the asymptotics (<a href="#A2.E38" title="Equation B.38 ‣ Lemma B.8. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.38</span></a>) as <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. According to Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx96" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.42)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z=\begin{cases}(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot ne^{\beta\rho}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z=\begin{cases}(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot ne^{\beta\rho}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">That is, when <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, the leading order terms are those terms involving <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ne^{\beta\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ne^{\beta\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, and all the remaining terms go to <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> after dividing <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ne^{\beta\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ne^{\beta\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>; when <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, the leading order terms are those terms involving <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and all the remaining terms go to <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> after dividing <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, when <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, the leading order term in (<a href="#A2.E37" title="Equation B.37 ‣ Lemma B.8. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.37</span></a>) is the term <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n^{3}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n^{3}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>; when <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, the leading order term is <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{2\beta}(d-1)n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{2\beta}(d-1)n</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves (<a href="#A2.E38" title="Equation B.38 ‣ Lemma B.8. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.38</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.9</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For terms <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{1},\mathbf{R}_{2},\mathbf{U}_{1},\mathbf{U}_{2},\mathbf{U}_{3},\mathbf{U}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{1},\mathbf{R}_{2},\mathbf{U}_{1},\mathbf{U}_{2},\mathbf{U}_{3},\mathbf{U}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.43)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})(\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4})\\
&amp;=\rho\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho)\\
&amp;\quad+\beta^{2}e^{3\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))^{2}(1-\rho)\\
&amp;\quad+\beta e^{\beta(2\rho+1)}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho)\\
&amp;\quad+\beta e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(\beta\rho+1)n(n-1)(1-\rho^{2})\\
&amp;\quad+\beta e^{3\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(\beta(1-\rho^{2})+(1-\rho)).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})(\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4})\\
&amp;=\rho\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho)\\
&amp;\quad+\beta^{2}e^{3\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))^{2}(1-\rho)\\
&amp;\quad+\beta e^{\beta(2\rho+1)}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho)\\
&amp;\quad+\beta e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(\beta\rho+1)n(n-1)(1-\rho^{2})\\
&amp;\quad+\beta e^{3\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(\beta(1-\rho^{2})+(1-\rho)).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As a corollary, when we pick <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following phase transition limits as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.44)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nZ^{3}}\sum_{i,j}(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})(\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4})=\begin{cases}\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)}{4}+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\\
0+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nZ^{3}}\sum_{i,j}(\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2})^{T}(\mathbf{R}_{1}+\mathbf{R}_{2})(\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4})=\begin{cases}\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)}{4}+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\\
0+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma B.9. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We expand each term in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma B.9. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a> and also apply Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma B.7. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a> to each term. We first estimate terms involving <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx99" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.45)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{1}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}\mathbf{U}_{3}=\sum_{i}\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\left(\mathbf{W}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}y_{i})\right)y_{i}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\sum_{i}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\mathbf{W}y_{i}=\rho\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\sum_{i}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\mathbf{V}\\
&amp;=\rho\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{1}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}\mathbf{U}_{3}=\sum_{i}\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\left(\mathbf{W}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}y_{i})\right)y_{i}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\sum_{i}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\mathbf{W}y_{i}=\rho\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\sum_{i}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\mathbf{V}\\
&amp;=\rho\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second and the third equality is because <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx100" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.46)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{1}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}\mathbf{U}_{4}=\sum_{i}\beta^{2}e^{3\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\left(\mathbf{W}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}y_{i})\right)\mathbf{V}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{3\beta\rho}\sum_{i}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{V}=\beta^{2}e^{3\beta\rho}(n\rho+(1-\rho))\sum_{i}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{3\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))^{2}(1-\rho),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{1}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}\mathbf{U}_{4}=\sum_{i}\beta^{2}e^{3\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\left(\mathbf{W}-y_{i}\otimes(\mathbf{W}y_{i})\right)\mathbf{V}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{3\beta\rho}\sum_{i}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\mathbf{W}\mathbf{V}=\beta^{2}e^{3\beta\rho}(n\rho+(1-\rho))\sum_{i}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{3\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))^{2}(1-\rho),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality is because <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx101" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.47)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{1}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\mathbf{U}_{3}=\sum_{i}\beta e^{\beta(\rho+1)}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{i})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)y_{i}=0,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{1}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\mathbf{U}_{3}=\sum_{i}\beta e^{\beta(\rho+1)}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{i})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)y_{i}=0,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality is because <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx102" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.48)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{1}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\mathbf{U}_{4}=\sum_{i}\beta e^{\beta(2\rho+1)}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\left((y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{i})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)\mathbf{V}\\
&amp;=\beta e^{\beta(2\rho+1)}\sum_{i}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\|^{2}=\beta e^{\beta(2\rho+1)}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{1}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\mathbf{U}_{4}=\sum_{i}\beta e^{\beta(2\rho+1)}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\right)^{T}\left((y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{i})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)\mathbf{V}\\
&amp;=\beta e^{\beta(2\rho+1)}\sum_{i}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\|^{2}=\beta e^{\beta(2\rho+1)}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality is because <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V},y_{i}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we estimate the terms involving <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We recall that <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{2}=\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{2}=\beta e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=j</annotation></semantics></math>, we can just replace <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\beta\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\beta\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, i,e, <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{2}=\beta e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{2}=\beta e^{\beta\rho}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.49)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{2}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}\mathbf{U}_{3}=0,\quad\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{2}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}\mathbf{U}_{4}=0,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>𝐑</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>𝐑</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>𝐔</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{2}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}\mathbf{U}_{3}=0,\quad\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{2}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}\mathbf{U}_{4}=0,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">because <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{2}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{2}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.50)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{2}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\mathbf{U}_{3}=\sum_{i,j}\beta e^{\beta(\rho+\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle)}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)^{T}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)y_{j}\\
&amp;=\beta e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\sum_{i\neq j}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)^{T}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\rho+y_{j}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(\beta\rho+1)\sum_{i\neq j}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\beta e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(\beta\rho+1)n(n-1)(1-\rho^{2}).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{2}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\mathbf{U}_{3}=\sum_{i,j}\beta e^{\beta(\rho+\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle)}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)^{T}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)y_{j}\\
&amp;=\beta e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\sum_{i\neq j}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)^{T}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\rho+y_{j}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(\beta\rho+1)\sum_{i\neq j}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\beta e^{2\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(\beta\rho+1)n(n-1)(1-\rho^{2}).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality is because <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> only when <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, on which <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle=\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, and the third equality is because <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j},y_{i}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j},y_{i}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx105" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.51)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{2}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\mathbf{U}_{4}=\sum_{i,j}\beta e^{\beta(2\rho+\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle)}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)^{T}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)\mathbf{V}\\
&amp;=\beta e^{3\beta\rho}\sum_{i\neq j}\left(\beta\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}(n\rho+(1-\rho))+\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)^{T}\mathbf{V}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta e^{3\beta\rho}\sum_{i\neq j}\left(\beta(1-\rho^{2})(n\rho+(1-\rho))+(1-\rho)(n\rho+(1-\rho))\right)\\
&amp;=\beta e^{3\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(\beta(1-\rho^{2})+(1-\rho)).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\mathbf{U}_{2}^{T}\mathbf{R}_{2}\mathbf{U}_{4}=\sum_{i,j}\beta e^{\beta(2\rho+\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle)}\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)^{T}\left((-y_{i}+\beta\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j})\otimes y_{i}+I_{d}\right)\mathbf{V}\\
&amp;=\beta e^{3\beta\rho}\sum_{i\neq j}\left(\beta\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}(n\rho+(1-\rho))+\left(\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\right)^{T}\mathbf{V}\right)\\
&amp;=\beta e^{3\beta\rho}\sum_{i\neq j}\left(\beta(1-\rho^{2})(n\rho+(1-\rho))+(1-\rho)(n\rho+(1-\rho))\right)\\
&amp;=\beta e^{3\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(\beta(1-\rho^{2})+(1-\rho)).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality is because <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> only when <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, on which <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle=\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, and the third equality is because <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j},y_{i}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j},y_{i}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof for (<a href="#A2.E44" title="Equation B.44 ‣ Lemma B.9. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.44</span></a>) is similar to the proof for (<a href="#A2.E38" title="Equation B.38 ‣ Lemma B.8. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.38</span></a>) in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>. Notice that when <math id="A2.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to pick up terms involving <math id="A2.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ne^{\beta\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ne^{\beta\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the leading order term in (<a href="#A2.E43" title="Equation B.43 ‣ Lemma B.9. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.43</span></a>) is the one in the second line of (<a href="#A2.E43" title="Equation B.43 ‣ Lemma B.9. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.43</span></a>), which is <math id="A2.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{2}n^{4}e^{3\beta\rho}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{2}n^{4}e^{3\beta\rho}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>; when <math id="A2.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, after diving <math id="A2.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nZ^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nZ^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, all terms in (<a href="#A2.E43" title="Equation B.43 ‣ Lemma B.9. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.43</span></a>) are <math id="A2.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> terms.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.10</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For terms <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{1},\mathbf{U}_{2},\mathbf{U}_{3},\mathbf{U}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{1},\mathbf{U}_{2},\mathbf{U}_{3},\mathbf{U}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx106" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.52)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\|\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+2)(1-\rho)\\
&amp;\quad\cdot\left[(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})^{2}+2e^{\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(n\rho+(1-\rho))+e^{2\beta\rho}n(n\rho+(1-\rho))\right].\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\|\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+2)(1-\rho)\\
&amp;\quad\cdot\left[(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})^{2}+2e^{\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(n\rho+(1-\rho))+e^{2\beta\rho}n(n\rho+(1-\rho))\right].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As a corollary, when we pick <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following phase transition limits as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx107" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.53)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nZ^{4}}\sum_{i,j}\|\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}=\begin{cases}\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{\beta^{2}\rho(1-\rho)(1+3\rho)}{16}+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
0+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nZ^{4}}\sum_{i,j}\|\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}=\begin{cases}\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
\frac{\beta^{2}\rho(1-\rho)(1+3\rho)}{16}+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}$},\\
0+o_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma B.10. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.10</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We notice that <math id="A2.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{U}_{1},\mathbf{U}_{2}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{U}_{1},\mathbf{U}_{2}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A2.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>. So,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.54)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\|\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2}\|^{2}=\delta_{ij}\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\|^{2}+\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\delta_{ij}\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho)+(1-\delta_{ij})\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(1-\rho^{2}),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\|\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2}\|^{2}=\delta_{ij}\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}\mathbf{V}\|^{2}+\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\delta_{ij}\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho)+(1-\delta_{ij})\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(1-\rho^{2}),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality is because <math id="A2.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{2\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{2\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> only if <math id="A2.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, on which <math id="A2.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{2\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}=e^{2\beta\rho}(1-\rho^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{2\beta\langle y_{j},y_{i}\rangle}\|\mathbf{P}_{y_{i}}y_{j}\|^{2}=e^{2\beta\rho}(1-\rho^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.55)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}=(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})^{2}+2e^{\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\langle\mathbf{V},y_{j}\rangle+e^{2\beta\rho}\|\mathbf{V}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})^{2}+2e^{\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(n\rho+(1-\rho))+e^{2\beta\rho}n(n\rho+(1-\rho)),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}=(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})^{2}+2e^{\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})\langle\mathbf{V},y_{j}\rangle+e^{2\beta\rho}\|\mathbf{V}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})^{2}+2e^{\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(n\rho+(1-\rho))+e^{2\beta\rho}n(n\rho+(1-\rho)),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is independent of <math id="A2.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx110" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(B.56)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\|\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\left[\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho)+n(n-1)\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(1-\rho^{2})\right]\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+2)(1-\rho)\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+2)(1-\rho)\\
&amp;\quad\cdot\left[(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})^{2}+2e^{\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(n\rho+(1-\rho))+e^{2\beta\rho}n(n\rho+(1-\rho))\right].\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\sum_{i,j}\|\mathbf{U}_{1}+\mathbf{U}_{2}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\left[\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+(1-\rho))(1-\rho)+n(n-1)\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}(1-\rho^{2})\right]\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+2)(1-\rho)\|\mathbf{U}_{3}+\mathbf{U}_{4}\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\beta^{2}e^{2\beta\rho}n(n-1)(n\rho+2)(1-\rho)\\
&amp;\quad\cdot\left[(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})^{2}+2e^{\beta\rho}(e^{\beta}-e^{\beta\rho})(n\rho+(1-\rho))+e^{2\beta\rho}n(n\rho+(1-\rho))\right].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof for (<a href="#A2.E53" title="Equation B.53 ‣ Lemma B.10. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.53</span></a>) is similar to the proof for (<a href="#A2.E38" title="Equation B.38 ‣ Lemma B.8. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.38</span></a>) in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>. Notice that when <math id="A2.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to pick up terms involving <math id="A2.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ne^{\beta\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ne^{\beta\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the leading order term in(<a href="#A2.E52" title="Equation B.52 ‣ Lemma B.10. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.52</span></a>) is is <math id="A2.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{2}n^{5}e^{4\beta\rho}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{2}n^{5}e^{4\beta\rho}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>; when <math id="A2.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, after diving <math id="A2.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nZ^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nZ^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, all terms in (<a href="#A2.E43" title="Equation B.43 ‣ Lemma B.9. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.43</span></a>) are <math id="A2.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> terms.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">As we have mentioned at the beginning of Appendix <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, we only need to focus the case when <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\leq\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\leq\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, which follows directly from Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>, Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma B.9. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>, and Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma B.10. ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.10</span></a>. We notice that, in these three lemmas, the leading order terms are the same, <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{2}\rho^{2}(1-\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>, which cancels in (<a href="#A2.E33" title="Equation B.33 ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.33</span></a>). Hence, when <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=0+o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{nd}\|\nabla_{X}X^{\prime}\|^{2}=0+o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, we also only need to use the corresponding cases in these three lemmas and combine them in (<a href="#A2.E33" title="Equation B.33 ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.33</span></a>) to get the conclusion in Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>. One remark is that under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 2.1. The simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have that <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq d</annotation></semantics></math> implicitly. So, when <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1}{1-\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, terms in (<a href="#A2.E33" title="Equation B.33 ‣ B.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.33</span></a>) involving <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\beta^{2}}{d}=\frac{\gamma^{2}(\log n)^{2}}{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\beta^{2}}{d}=\frac{\gamma^{2}(\log n)^{2}}{d}</annotation></semantics></math> also become <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Modified Assumptions with More Median Phases</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we modify Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, so that we can prove the existence of three different phases like Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>. We remark that we only showed the existence of two phases (two extrema) in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2.3. Propagation of Gradients under Attention Layer ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>, but it doesn’t mean under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, there is no other transition phase between these two phases (two extrema). Under the following Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ Appendix C Modified Assumptions with More Median Phases ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we can show there are indeed at least three phases. Recall that for any <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>, we defined <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}=N(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}=N(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span></span><span id="Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}\|^{2}\in[q_{1},q_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}\|^{2}\in[q_{1},q_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for some positive constants </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}\leq q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}\leq q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, four positive constants </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{3},\rho_{4},\kappa_{3},\kappa_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{3},\rho_{4},\kappa_{3},\kappa_{4}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{3}\leq\rho_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{3}\leq\rho_{4}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{3}\leq\kappa_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{3}\leq\kappa_{4}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{4}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{4}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, such that for any </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, if we define</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx111" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{K}_{i}=\left\{m\neq i\ |\ \langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle\in[\rho_{3},\rho_{4}]\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{K}_{i}=\left\{m\neq i\ |\ \langle y_{m},y_{i}\rangle\in[\rho_{3},\rho_{4}]\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then we have that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx112" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\kappa_{3}\leq\frac{\left|\mathcal{K}_{i}\right|}{n^{\tau}}\leq\kappa_{4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\kappa_{3}\leq\frac{\left|\mathcal{K}_{i}\right|}{n^{\tau}}\leq\kappa_{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any </span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and any </span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle\in[\rho_{1},\rho_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y_{i},y_{j}\rangle\in[\rho_{1},\rho_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for some nonnegative constants </span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{1},\rho_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{1},\rho_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying </span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{1}\leq\rho_{2}&lt;\rho_{3}\leq\rho_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{1}\leq\rho_{2}&lt;\rho_{3}\leq\rho_{4}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For technical reason, we further assume that </span><math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\tau)(1-\rho_{2})+\rho_{2}&lt;\rho_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\tau)(1-\rho_{2})+\rho_{2}&lt;\rho_{3}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant. Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>), for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{i}=\begin{cases}(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot\left(\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}e^{a_{im}}\right)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\min\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}},\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{4}-\rho_{1}}\right\}$},\\
(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot\left(\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}e^{a_{im}}\right)&amp;\text{if $\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{3}-\rho_{2}}&lt;\gamma&lt;\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{3}}$},\\
(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\max\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}},\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{4}}\right\}$},\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{i}=\begin{cases}(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot\left(\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}e^{a_{im}}\right)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\min\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}},\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{4}-\rho_{1}}\right\}$},\\
(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot\left(\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}e^{a_{im}}\right)&amp;\text{if $\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{3}-\rho_{2}}&lt;\gamma&lt;\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{3}}$},\\
(1+o_{n}(1))\cdot e^{\beta}&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\max\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}},\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{4}}\right\}$},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the terms <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> go to <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> with speeds independent of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> but only depending on <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho_{1},\rho_{2},\rho_{3},\rho_{4},\tau,\kappa_{3},\kappa_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho_{1},\rho_{2},\rho_{3},\rho_{4},\tau,\kappa_{3},\kappa_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is similar to Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. We notice that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx114" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}Z_{i}&amp;=e^{\beta}+\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}e^{a_{im}}+\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}e^{a_{im}}\\
&amp;=n^{\gamma}+\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}+\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}Z_{i}&amp;=e^{\beta}+\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}e^{a_{im}}+\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}e^{a_{im}}\\
&amp;=n^{\gamma}+\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}+\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We also notice that <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{3}n^{\tau}\leq|\mathcal{K}_{i}|\leq\kappa_{4}n^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{3}n^{\tau}\leq|\mathcal{K}_{i}|\leq\kappa_{4}n^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> according to Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ Appendix C Modified Assumptions with More Median Phases ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx115" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\kappa_{3}n^{\tau+\gamma\rho_{3}}\leq|\mathcal{K}_{i}|\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{3}}\leq\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\leq|\mathcal{K}_{i}|\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{4}}\leq\kappa_{4}n^{\tau+\gamma\rho_{4}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\kappa_{3}n^{\tau+\gamma\rho_{3}}\leq|\mathcal{K}_{i}|\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{3}}\leq\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\leq|\mathcal{K}_{i}|\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{4}}\leq\kappa_{4}n^{\tau+\gamma\rho_{4}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx116" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(n-\kappa_{4}n^{\tau}-1)\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{1}}\leq\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\leq(n-|\mathcal{K}_{i}|-1)\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{2}}\leq n^{1+\gamma\rho_{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(n-\kappa_{4}n^{\tau}-1)\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{1}}\leq\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}\leq(n-|\mathcal{K}_{i}|-1)\cdot n^{\gamma\rho_{2}}\leq n^{1+\gamma\rho_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\min\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}},\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{4}-\rho_{1}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\min\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}},\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{4}-\rho_{1}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the leading order term in <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math>; when <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{3}-\rho_{2}}&lt;\gamma&lt;\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{3}-\rho_{2}}&lt;\gamma&lt;\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the leading order term in <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}n^{\gamma\langle y_{i},y_{m}\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math>; when <math id="A3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\max\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}},\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{4}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\max\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}},\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{4}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the leading order term in <math id="A3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also remark that the last assumption in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ Appendix C Modified Assumptions with More Median Phases ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is to ensure the existence of the middle phase, i.e., <math id="A3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{3}-\rho_{2}}&lt;\gamma&lt;\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{3}-\rho_{2}}&lt;\gamma&lt;\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This finishes the proof for Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Modified Assumptions with More Median Phases ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> by similar arguments as in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem and Theorem ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A direct corollary of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Modified Assumptions with More Median Phases ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> is the following theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 2.2. The almost-simplex case ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>) we have the following phase transition phenomena: let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\gamma\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\gamma\log n</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant. For any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\llbracket 1,n\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> the updating dynamics (<a href="#S2.E3" title="Equation 2.3 ‣ 2. A phase transition for attention ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>) can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx117" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(C.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}^{\prime}=\alpha x_{i}+\begin{cases}\frac{\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}e^{a_{im}}y_{m}}{\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}e^{a_{im}}}+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\min\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}},\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{4}-\rho_{1}}\right\}$},\\
\frac{\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}e^{a_{im}}y_{m}}{\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}e^{a_{im}}}+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{3}-\rho_{2}}&lt;\gamma&lt;\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{3}}$},\\
y_{i}+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\max\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}},\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{4}}\right\}$},\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}^{\prime}=\alpha x_{i}+\begin{cases}\frac{\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}e^{a_{im}}y_{m}}{\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{K}_{i}\cup\{i\}}e^{a_{im}}}+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&lt;\min\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{1}},\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{4}-\rho_{1}}\right\}$},\\
\frac{\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}e^{a_{im}}y_{m}}{\sum_{m\in\mathcal{K}_{i}}e^{a_{im}}}+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\frac{1-\tau}{\rho_{3}-\rho_{2}}&lt;\gamma&lt;\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{3}}$},\\
y_{i}+\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)&amp;\text{if $\gamma&gt;\max\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho_{2}},\frac{\tau}{1-\rho_{4}}\right\}$},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The terms <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{o}_{n}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> represent vectors in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.338em;" width="0.338em"><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm I}\kern-1.79993pt{\rm R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with norms going to <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, with a speed independent of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> but only depending on <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\rho_{1},\rho_{2},\rho_{3},\rho_{4},\tau,\kappa_{3},\kappa_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\rho_{1},\rho_{2},\rho_{3},\rho_{4},\tau,\kappa_{3},\kappa_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem C.2. ‣ Appendix C Modified Assumptions with More Median Phases ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> is similar to Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Modified Assumptions with More Median Phases ‣ Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> so we omit its proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
